{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc | sed -n '280,640p'\"","aggregated_output":"   280\t   round-order on the cell is preserved on the resumer (S7.4.3).\n   281\t   The call's `:op` rides when the entry carries it (the engine's\n   282\t   own response wait does not; a caller assembling the frame takes\n   283\t   it from the call's parked record).\"\n   284\t  [resources mint codec entry]\n   285\t  (if-let [cell (cursor-cell resources entry)]\n   286\t    (if-let [cid (mint codec (:id cell)\n   287\t                       (get resources (:stream-id cell))\n   288\t                       (:cursor cell))]\n   289\t      {:pending (cond-> {:yin.k/reason :ffi,\n   290\t                         :yin.k/call-id (:call-id entry),\n   291\t                         :yin.k/cell cid}\n   292\t                  (contains? entry :op) (assoc :yin.k/op (:op entry))),\n   293\t       :cell? true}\n   294\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity (get resources (:stream-id cell)))))\n   295\t    (unsatisfied)))\n   296\t\n   297\t\n   298\t(defn- lift-write\n   299\t  \"S7.4.3's blocked write: the target stream's marker and the\n   300\t   retained `:datom` -- the value a retry appends, without which the\n   301\t   wait is not re-establishable. A put names a stream, never a\n   302\t   cursor cell.\"\n   303\t  [serve! resources entry]\n   304\t  (let [h (get resources (:stream-id entry))]\n   305\t    (if-let [marker (lift-marker serve! h)]\n   306\t      {:pending {:yin.k/reason :put,\n   307\t                 :yin.k/stream marker,\n   308\t                 :yin.k/value (:datom entry)}}\n   309\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity h)))))\n   310\t\n   311\t\n   312\t(defn- call-out-cell\n   313\t  \"The emitter's call-out cursor cell -- the response route the\n   314\t   retained call had on the emitter, carried as a cell like any\n   315\t   other: the cursor entry under `vm/call-out-cursor-key`, reading\n   316\t   the call-out stream under `vm/call-out-stream-key` at its kept\n   317\t   position. It lowers under its own fresh key (S7.5.3), so a\n   318\t   response wait on the same call-out cursor shares it and distinct\n   319\t   routes stay distinct. nil when the composition holds no call\n   320\t   pair, which no real retained request does -- the pair is checked\n   321\t   before the call parked.\"\n   322\t  [resources]\n   323\t  (let [cursor (get resources vm/call-out-cursor-key)\n   324\t        handle (get resources vm/call-out-stream-key)]\n   325\t    (when (and (map? cursor) (contains? cursor :stream-id) handle)\n   326\t      {:id vm/call-out-cursor-key,\n   327\t       :stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key,\n   328\t       :cursor (:cursor cursor)})))\n   329\t\n   330\t\n   331\t(defn- lift-retained-request\n   332\t  \"S7.4.3's retained call: a `:put` entry carrying `:request-sent`,\n   333\t   the request the engine holds unsent. The request stream's marker\n   334\t   is served, and `:request-op` and `:request-args` are read out of\n   335\t   the retained envelope so a resumer rebuilds it verbatim under the\n   336\t   call id. The emitter's call-out cursor rides beside them as a cell\n   337\t   (`call-out-cell`) at its kept position -- the response route the\n   338\t   call had on the emitter -- and lowers under its own fresh key like\n   339\t   any cell, never at a fixed key. `:yin.k/unsatisfied` when the\n   340\t   request stream cannot be served, or the route is missing or its\n   341\t   cursor does not survive the codec round trip.\"\n   342\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\n   343\t  (let [h (get resources (:stream-id entry))\n   344\t        envelope (:datom entry)\n   345\t        route (call-out-cell resources)]\n   346\t    (if-let [cid (when route\n   347\t                   (mint codec (:id route)\n   348\t                         (get resources (:stream-id route))\n   349\t                         (:cursor route)))]\n   350\t      (if-let [marker (lift-marker serve! h)]\n   351\t        {:pending {:yin.k/reason :ffi-request,\n   352\t                   :yin.k/call-id (:call-id entry),\n   353\t                   :yin.k/request-op (or (apply2/request-op envelope)\n   354\t                                         (:op entry)),\n   355\t                   :yin.k/request-args (apply2/request-args envelope),\n   356\t                   :yin.k/request marker,\n   357\t                   :yin.k/response-cell cid},\n   358\t         :cell? true}\n   359\t        (unsatisfied (local-identity h)))\n   360\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity\n   361\t                     (or (and route (get resources (:stream-id route)))\n   362\t                         h))))))\n   363\t\n   364\t\n   365\t(defn- lift-link\n   366\t  \"S7.4.3's link variants: the link pair name the engine's own fixed\n   367\t   link keys on a real entry (`module/link-request-resource` and\n   368\t   `module/link-response-resource`), resolved into `:resources`, and\n   369\t   the kept `:cursor` on the response stream\n   370\t   (`module/require-handler` mints it before the envelope is appended)\n   371\t   is the response cell -- a cell like any other, at its kept\n   372\t   position. Both pair markers travel, the engine's `:link-response`\n   373\t   entry retaining its `:request` beside the response side; the\n   374\t   envelope rides verbatim on the request-in-hand variant.\"\n   375\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\n   376\t  (let [reason (:reason entry)\n   377\t        resp-h (get resources (:response entry))\n   378\t        req-h (get resources (:request entry))\n   379\t        kept (:cursor entry)]\n   380\t    (if-let [cid (mint codec [(:response entry) kept] resp-h kept)]\n   381\t      (let [resp (lift-marker serve! resp-h)\n   382\t            req (lift-marker serve! req-h)]\n   383\t        (if (and resp req)\n   384\t          {:pending (cond-> {:yin.k/reason reason,\n   385\t                             :yin.k/link-id (:link-id entry),\n   386\t                             :yin.k/name (:name entry),\n   387\t                             :yin.k/request req,\n   388\t                             :yin.k/response resp,\n   389\t                             :yin.k/cell cid}\n   390\t                      (= :link-request reason)\n   391\t                      (assoc :yin.k/envelope (:envelope entry))),\n   392\t           :cell? true}\n   393\t          (unsatisfied (local-identity (or req-h resp-h)))))\n   394\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity resp-h)))))\n   395\t\n   396\t\n   397\t(defn- lift-one\n   398\t  \"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lifted into `{:pending data,\n   399\t   :cell? bool}` -- `:cell?` true when the variant names a cursor\n   400\t   cell, which is what puts `:dao.stream.remote/v1` in\n   401\t   `:yin.k/cursor-profiles` -- or an outcome carrying\n   402\t   `:yin.k/status`: `:yin.k/unsatisfied` when a stream cannot be\n   403\t   served or a kept cursor does not survive the codec round trip;\n   404\t   `:yin.k/undecodable`, naming the reason, when the entry is no\n   405\t   variant at all.\"\n   406\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\n   407\t  (case (:reason entry)\n   408\t    :next\n   409\t    (if (:call-id entry)\n   410\t      (lift-response-wait resources mint codec entry)\n   411\t      (lift-read resources mint codec entry))\n   412\t\n   413\t    :put\n   414\t    (if (:request-sent entry)\n   415\t      (lift-retained-request serve! resources mint codec entry)\n   416\t      (lift-write serve! resources entry))\n   417\t\n   418\t    :link-request (lift-link serve! resources mint codec entry)\n   419\t\n   420\t    :link-response (lift-link serve! resources mint codec entry)\n   421\t\n   422\t    :install\n   423\t    {:pending {:yin.k/reason :install, :yin.k/name (:name entry)}}\n   424\t\n   425\t    {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable, :yin.k/reason (:reason entry)}))\n   426\t\n   427\t\n   428\t;; =============================================================================\n   429\t;; Lift: the frame and the single entry\n   430\t;; =============================================================================\n   431\t\n   432\t(defn lift-frame\n   433\t  \"A whole frame set of S7.4.3 pending entries, lifted together:\n   434\t   `{:yin.k/pending [data ...], :yin.k/cells {cell-id cell},\n   435\t   :yin.k/requires requires}` on success -- the cells minted across\n   436\t   the WHOLE set, so two waiters on one engine cursor cell lift to\n   437\t   one UCF cell (S7.5.3) and `:dao.stream.remote/v1` rides in\n   438\t   `:yin.k/cursor-profiles` when any entry names a cell; the S7.9\n   439\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` outcome, naming the stream identity where one\n   440\t   is known, when any entry's stream cannot be served or its kept\n   441\t   cursor does not survive the codec round trip; the S7.9\n   442\t   `:yin.k/undecodable` outcome when any entry names no variant.\n   443\t   Failure is total (S7.5.4): a refused leaf refuses the frame.\"\n   444\t  ([serve! resources entries]\n   445\t   (lift-frame serve! resources entries cursor-codec))\n   446\t  ([serve! resources entries codec]\n   447\t   (let [found (atom {:cells {}, :of {}})\n   448\t         mint (mint-cell serve! found)\n   449\t         lifted (mapv #(lift-one serve! resources mint codec %) entries)]\n   450\t     (if-let [refusal (some #(when (contains? % :yin.k/status) %) lifted)]\n   451\t       refusal\n   452\t       {:yin.k/pending (mapv :pending lifted),\n   453\t        :yin.k/cells (:cells @found),\n   454\t        :yin.k/requires (if (some :cell? lifted) requires {})}))))\n   455\t\n   456\t\n   457\t(defn lift-pending\n   458\t  \"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lifted into its own self-contained\n   459\t   cell table: `{:yin.k/pending data, :yin.k/cells {cell-id cell},\n   460\t   :yin.k/requires requires}` on success, with the same `:yin.k/\n   461\t   unsatisfied` and `:yin.k/undecodable` outcomes `lift-frame`\n   462\t   gives. Frame assembly that shares cells across entries is\n   463\t   `lift-frame`'s.\"\n   464\t  ([serve! resources entry]\n   465\t   (lift-pending serve! resources entry cursor-codec))\n   466\t  ([serve! resources entry codec]\n   467\t   (let [r (lift-frame serve! resources [entry] codec)]\n   468\t     (if (contains? r :yin.k/status)\n   469\t       r\n   470\t       (assoc r :yin.k/pending (first (:yin.k/pending r)))))))\n   471\t\n   472\t\n   473\t;; =============================================================================\n   474\t;; Lower: back into resources and a wait-set entry\n   475\t;; =============================================================================\n   476\t\n   477\t(defn- stream-id-of\n   478\t  \"The fresh resource id the reflection of the stream `identity`\n   479\t   names stands under: derived from the identity, so two markers of\n   480\t   one stream attach once and lower shared. A receiver composing\n   481\t   these entries into a live `:resources` table re-keys them -- the\n   482\t   ids are fresh for the lowered state, the remap mechanical.\"\n   483\t  [identity]\n   484\t  (keyword \"yin.k\" (str \"s-\" identity)))\n   485\t\n   486\t\n   487\t(defn- pending-markers\n   488\t  \"Every stream marker `pending` names beside its cells' -- the\n   489\t   target of a put, the request of a retained call, the pair of a\n   490\t   link request.\"\n   491\t  [pending]\n   492\t  (case (:yin.k/reason pending)\n   493\t    :put [(:yin.k/stream pending)]\n   494\t    :ffi-request [(:yin.k/request pending)]\n   495\t    (:link-request :link-response)\n   496\t    [(:yin.k/request pending)\n   497\t     (:yin.k/response pending)]\n   498\t    []))\n   499\t\n   500\t\n   501\t(defn- attach-all\n   502\t  \"One attach per distinct stream identity, each ok installing its\n   503\t   reflection under `stream-id-of`'s fresh resource id. The first\n   504\t   attach that does not answer ok -- a reflection marked gone\n   505\t   included -- refuses the lower as `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming that\n   506\t   identity.\"\n   507\t  [attach! markers]\n   508\t  (let [by-id (reduce (fn [m mkr]\n   509\t                        (update m (:dao.stream/identity mkr) #(or % mkr)))\n   510\t                      {} markers)]\n   511\t    (reduce-kv (fn [acc identity mkr]\n   512\t                 (if-let [h (lower-marker attach! mkr)]\n   513\t                   (let [sid (stream-id-of identity)]\n   514\t                     (-> acc\n   515\t                         (assoc-in [:streams identity] sid)\n   516\t                         (assoc-in [:resources sid] h)))\n   517\t                   (reduced (unsatisfied identity))))\n   518\t               {:streams {}, :resources {}}\n   519\t               by-id)))\n   520\t\n   521\t\n   522\t(defn- cell-resources\n   523\t  \"The fresh cursor entry each UCF cell lowers to: its carried\n   524\t   position, on the reflection of the stream the cell names, under\n   525\t   the cell id itself -- two references to one cell share the one\n   526\t   entry, and one ref per cell keeps its own (S7.5.3). A response\n   527\t   route is no exception: it lowers under its own fresh key, never\n   528\t   at a fixed key, so distinct routes stay distinct and no migrated\n   529\t   route can ever misroute a new call.\"\n   530\t  [streams cells]\n   531\t  (into {}\n   532\t        (map (fn [[cid cell]]\n   533\t               [cid {:stream-id (streams (cell-identity cells cid)),\n   534\t                     :cursor (:yin.k/position cell)}]))\n   535\t        cells))\n   536\t\n   537\t\n   538\t(defn- link-pair-resources\n   539\t  \"The engine's fixed link keys (`module/link-request-resource`,\n   540\t   `module/link-response-resource`) mapped onto the reflections a\n   541\t   lowered link wait uses: the engine's sweep retries a\n   542\t   `:link-request` by appending at the fixed request key\n   543\t   (`module/append-link-request`) and polls a `:link-response` at the\n   544\t   fixed response key (`poll-link-response`), so a lowered link wait\n   545\t   parks where the engine looks. One pair per task: the identity of\n   546\t   each side rides the pending's own markers.\"\n   547\t  [streams resources pendings]\n   548\t  (reduce (fn [acc pending]\n   549\t            (if (contains? #{:link-request :link-response}\n   550\t                           (:yin.k/reason pending))\n   551\t              (let [req-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\n   552\t                                            :dao.stream/identity])\n   553\t                    resp-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/response\n   554\t                                             :dao.stream/identity])\n   555\t                    req (get resources (streams req-id))\n   556\t                    resp (get resources (streams resp-id))]\n   557\t                (if (and req resp)\n   558\t                  (assoc acc\n   559\t                         module/link-request-resource req,\n   560\t                         module/link-response-resource resp)\n   561\t                  acc))\n   562\t              acc))\n   563\t          {}\n   564\t          pendings))\n   565\t\n   566\t\n   567\t(defn- lower-one\n   568\t  \"One pending of S7.4.3, lowered: `{:entry e}` -- the wait-set\n   569\t   entry the receiver parks, the caller's register context `ctx`\n   570\t   merged verbatim under the stream and cell fields the data\n   571\t   rebuilds -- or an outcome carrying `:yin.k/status`, naming the\n   572\t   stream identity where one is known. A wait's `:cursor-ref` names\n   573\t   its cell's own fresh key, so migrated waits poll routes no new\n   574\t   call shares.\"\n   575\t  [pending ctx streams cells]\n   576\t  (case (:yin.k/reason pending)\n   577\t    :next\n   578\t    (let [cid (:yin.k/cell pending)]\n   579\t      (if-let [sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))]\n   580\t        {:entry (merge ctx\n   581\t                       {:reason :next,\n   582\t                        :stream-id sid,\n   583\t                        :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cid}})}\n   584\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\n   585\t\n   586\t    :put\n   587\t    (if-let [sid (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/stream\n   588\t                                           :dao.stream/identity]))]\n   589\t      {:entry (merge ctx\n   590\t                     {:reason :put,\n   591\t                      :stream-id sid,\n   592\t                      :datom (:yin.k/value pending)})}\n   593\t      (unsatisfied (get-in pending [:yin.k/stream :dao.stream/identity])))\n   594\t\n   595\t    :ffi\n   596\t    (let [cid (:yin.k/cell pending)]\n   597\t      (if-let [sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))]\n   598\t        {:entry (merge ctx\n   599\t                       (cond-> {:reason :next,\n   600\t                                :call-id (:yin.k/call-id pending),\n   601\t                                :stream-id sid,\n   602\t                                :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cid}}\n   603\t                         (contains? pending :yin.k/op)\n   604\t                         (assoc :op (:yin.k/op pending))))}\n   605\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\n   606\t\n   607\t    :ffi-request\n   608\t    (let [req-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\n   609\t                                  :dao.stream/identity])\n   610\t          route-id (cell-identity cells (:yin.k/response-cell\n   611\t                                          pending))]\n   612\t      (if (and (streams req-id) (streams route-id))\n   613\t        {:entry (merge ctx\n   614\t                       {:reason :put,\n   615\t                        :request-sent true,\n   616\t                        :call-id (:yin.k/call-id pending),\n   617\t                        :op (:yin.k/request-op pending),\n   618\t                        :stream-id vm/call-in-stream-key,\n   619\t                        :datom (apply2/request (:yin.k/call-id pending)\n   620\t                                               (:yin.k/request-op\n   621\t                                                 pending)\n   622\t                                               (:yin.k/request-args\n   623\t                                                 pending))})}\n   624\t        (unsatisfied (if (streams req-id) route-id req-id))))\n   625\t\n   626\t    (:link-request :link-response)\n   627\t    (let [reason (:yin.k/reason pending)\n   628\t          cid (:yin.k/cell pending)\n   629\t          sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))\n   630\t          req (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\n   631\t                                        :dao.stream/identity]))]\n   632\t      (if (and sid req)\n   633\t        {:entry (merge ctx\n   634\t                       (cond-> {:reason reason,\n   635\t                                :link-id (:yin.k/link-id pending),\n   636\t                                :name (:yin.k/name pending),\n   637\t                                :request module/link-request-resource,\n   638\t                                :response module/link-response-resource,\n   639\t                                :cursor (:yin.k/position (get cells cid))}\n   640\t                         (= :link-request reason)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '345,390p;510,565p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '450,490p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '345,390p;510,565p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '450,490p'\"","aggregated_output":"   345\t\n   346\t\n   347\t(defn make-woken-run-queue-entries\n   348\t  \"Transform woken wait-set entries into ready-queue entries.\n   349\t   Readers (with :cursor-ref) record the successor cursor the transport\n   350\t   returned as a resource update. Writers (no :cursor-ref) just stamp\n   351\t   :value. Each woken result's :status rides onto the ready entry, where\n   352\t   terminal-resume-outcome reads it.\n   353\t\n   354\t   A woken status the immediate `handle-put`/`handle-next` answers as the\n   355\t   shaped refusal -- `:dao.stream/refused`, or an outcome outside this\n   356\t   contract version -- is shaped into that same refusal value, so whether\n   357\t   the first attempt blocked does not change what the program sees. The\n   358\t   declared error outcomes stay raw, for terminal-resume-outcome to raise.\n   359\t\n   360\t   The ready entry stays pure data: any `:stream` handle a poll resolved\n   361\t   is dropped -- the resource updates carry the successor cursor, and\n   362\t   handles are re-resolved from ids when needed again -- so an entry\n   363\t   neither waits nor runs holding a host object.\"\n   364\t  [state woken]\n   365\t  (mapv (fn [{:keys [entry value cursor status], :as woken-entry}]\n   366\t          (let [cursor-ref (:cursor-ref entry)\n   367\t                value (if (wake-refusal? (:reason entry) status)\n   368\t                        (cond-> {:status :refused\n   369\t                                 :outcome status\n   370\t                                 :stream-id (:stream-id entry)}\n   371\t                          cursor-ref (assoc :cursor-id (:id cursor-ref)))\n   372\t                        value)\n   373\t                updates\n   374\t                (or (:resource-updates woken-entry)\n   375\t                    (when (and cursor-ref cursor)\n   376\t                      (let [cursor-id (:id cursor-ref)\n   377\t                            cursor-data (get (:resources state) cursor-id)]\n   378\t                        {cursor-id (assoc cursor-data :cursor cursor)})))]\n   379\t            (dissoc (assoc entry\n   380\t                           :value value\n   381\t                           :resource-updates updates\n   382\t                           :status status\n   383\t                           :cursor cursor)\n   384\t                    :stream)))\n   385\t        woken))\n   386\t\n   387\t\n   388\t(defn handle-make\n   389\t  \"Handle :stream/make. Creates a stream through the composition's\n   390\t   `:make-stream`, holds the handle in the private `:resources` table, and\n   510\t  \"The engine's composition for `dao.stream.waitset/check`: the whole\n   511\t   resolver contract in one value, both functions synchronous and pure over\n   512\t   the immutable resources table. Neither touches a transport -- the\n   513\t   library polls, the engine maps.\n   514\t\n   515\t   `:resolve` maps one whole parked entry to its live handle plus the\n   516\t   cursor to read from -- or the value to append -- out of the VM's\n   517\t   `:resources`. The cursor is re-resolved on every round even when an\n   518\t   earlier round baked a value into the entry: another waiter on the same\n   519\t   cursor-ref may have advanced the cell since. `:advance` commits a woken\n   520\t   reader's successor -- or recovery -- cursor to its cell before later\n   521\t   entries resolve, so a shared cursor-ref advances within the round.\"\n   522\t  {:resolve (fn [resources entry]\n   523\t              (if-let [cursor-ref (:cursor-ref entry)]\n   524\t                (let [cursor-data (get resources (:id cursor-ref))]\n   525\t                  {:stream (or (:stream entry)\n   526\t                               (get resources (:stream-id cursor-data)))\n   527\t                   :cursor (:cursor cursor-data)})\n   528\t                {:stream (or (:stream entry) (get resources (:stream-id entry)))\n   529\t                 :value (:datom entry)}))\n   530\t   :advance (fn [resources entry cursor]\n   531\t              (let [cursor-id (:id (:cursor-ref entry))]\n   532\t                (if cursor-id\n   533\t                  (assoc-in resources [cursor-id :cursor] cursor)\n   534\t                  resources)))})\n   535\t\n   536\t\n   537\t;; =============================================================================\n   538\t;; Lift and lower: the portable encoding a linked slice crosses in\n   539\t;; (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, acts 1 and 4; UCF section 7.5.1)\n   540\t;; =============================================================================\n   541\t\n   542\t(defn- non-portable!\n   543\t  [kind data]\n   544\t  (fail \"Value is not portable\"\n   545\t        (merge data {:yin.k/status :yin.k/non-portable, :yin.k/kind kind})))\n   546\t\n   547\t\n   548\t(defn- scalar?\n   549\t  [x]\n   550\t  (or (nil? x) (boolean? x) (number? x) (string? x) (keyword? x)\n   551\t      (symbol? x)))\n   552\t\n   553\t\n   554\t(defn- encode-primitive\n   555\t  \"A host function as UCF 7.5.2's primitive marker: its one name in\n   556\t   `vm`'s primitives, with that name's profile address.\"\n   557\t  [vm f]\n   558\t  (let [n (vm/name-of (:primitives vm)\n   559\t                      (or (:primitive-canonical-names vm) {})\n   560\t                      f)\n   561\t        profile (when (symbol? n) (vm/profile-of (:primitives vm) n))]\n   562\t    (cond\n   563\t      (nil? n) (non-portable! :unnamed-function {})\n   564\t      (not (symbol? n)) (non-portable! :ambiguous-primitive {})\n   565\t      (= :host (:yin.k/class profile))\n   450\t                         (update :wait-set (fnil conj [])\n   451\t                                 (response-wait-entry seg (inc pc) E St' K\n   452\t                                                      call-id))\n   453\t                         (assoc :control nil\n   454\t                                :k nil\n   455\t                                :value :yin/blocked\n   456\t                                :blocked? true\n   457\t                                :halted? false))\n   458\t                     :dao.stream/full\n   459\t                     (-> parked\n   460\t                         (update :wait-set (fnil conj [])\n   461\t                                 {:segment seg, :pc (inc pc),\n   462\t                                  :env E, :stack St', :k K,\n   463\t                                  :request-sent true,\n   464\t                                  :call-id call-id,\n   465\t                                  :op ffi-op,\n   466\t                                  :reason :put,\n   467\t                                  :stream-id vm/call-in-stream-key,\n   468\t                                  :datom request})\n   469\t                         (assoc :control nil\n   470\t                                :k nil\n   471\t                                :value :yin/blocked\n   472\t                                :blocked? true\n   473\t                                :halted? false))\n   474\t                     (throw (ex-info \"FFI request could not be appended\"\n   475\t                                     {:op ffi-op,\n   476\t                                      :outcome (or (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n   477\t                                                   (:dao.stream.apply/outcome\n   478\t                                                     result))}))))\n   479\t              ;; No decoded image holds another opcode (:move stays unused)\n   480\t              (throw (ex-info \"Unknown opcode in segment\"\n   481\t                              {:op op, :segment seg, :pc pc})))))))))\n   482\t\n   483\t\n   484\t;; =============================================================================\n   485\t;; Scheduler\n   486\t;; =============================================================================\n   487\t\n   488\t(defn- scheduler-round\n   489\t  \"One round between continuations: poll the wait set, then run whatever\n   490\t   woke. Entries here carry no :resume, so `engine/resume-from-run-queue`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
