ollab/1790536094287-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice8-confirm-r3.gpt-6-sol.prompt.md\\n?? collab/1790536094287-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice8-confirm-r3.gpt-6-sol.stdout.log\\n?? collab/1790539547222-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice8-confirm-r4.gpt-6-sol.prompt.md\\n?? collab/1790539547222-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice8-confirm-r4.gpt-6-sol.stdout.log\\n?? collab/1790539586724-architect-slice7-confirm.gpt-6-sol.prompt.md\\n?? collab/1790539586724-architect-slice7-confirm.gpt-6-sol.stdout.log\\n?? collab/1790543968849-architect-slice5-gate-r2.gpt-6-sol.prompt.md\\n?? collab/1790543968849-architect-slice5-gate-r2.gpt-6-sol.stdout.log\\n?? collab/1790543994308-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice8-confirm-r5.gpt-6-sol.prompt.md\\n?? collab/1790543994308-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice8-confirm-r5.gpt-6-sol.stdout.log\\n?? collab/slice5-r3-jvm-full-2.log\\n?? collab/slice5-r3-jvm-full.log\\n?? collab/slice5-r3-node.log\\n?? public/chp/blog/muse-ai-agent-on-datom-world.blog\\n?? src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc\\n?? test/dao/stream/ws_project_cross_jvm_test.clj\\n?? test/dao/stream/ws_project_cross_node_test.cljs\\n?? test/dao/stream/ws_project_peer.cljc\\n?? test/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj\\n?? test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc\\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-09-27 20:07:00 GMT\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-28 03:07:00 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\\n\\n**P1 — the response route still occupies the receiver’s fixed cursor key.** The fix preserves the receiver’s call-in and call-out stream keys, and the retained retry uses a fresh reflection key ([remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:637)). But lowering installs the emitter’s response cell at `vm/call-out-cursor-key` ([remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:524)), which the engine also uses for every new call’s response wait ([semantic.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:106)). The engine resolves that wait through the cursor cell’s stream, so a new call’s response wait initially reads the emitter’s call-out ([engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:522)).\\n\\nThe two-call test reaches completion only after it manually replaces that cursor cell with the receiver’s own at lines 565–567 ([remote_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:559)). No slice 8 code performs that handoff. Replacing the cell can also redirect a co-waiter still sharing the migrated response cell, contrary to the cell-sharing rule ([design](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:916)). The test therefore does not establish correct routing for both waits without composition intervention.\\n\\nI did not edit files or rerun suites. I accept the supplied 18-test, 162-assertion results on JVM, Node, and Dart as evidence for the tested path.\\n\\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\\nSign-off: DENIED\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc | sed -n '460,700p'; nl -ba test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc | sed -n '430,640p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | sed -n '545,630p;900,930p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc | sed -n '460,700p'; nl -ba test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc | sed -n '430,640p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | sed -n '545,630p;900,930p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   460\\t  \\\"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lifted into its own self-contained\\n   461\\t   cell table: `{:yin.k/pending data, :yin.k/cells {cell-id cell},\\n   462\\t   :yin.k/requires requires}` on success, with the same `:yin.k/\\n   463\\t   unsatisfied` and `:yin.k/undecodable` outcomes `lift-frame`\\n   464\\t   gives. Frame assembly that shares cells across entries is\\n   465\\t   `lift-frame`'s.\\\"\\n   466\\t  ([serve! resources entry]\\n   467\\t   (lift-pending serve! resources entry cursor-codec))\\n   468\\t  ([serve! resources entry codec]\\n   469\\t   (let [r (lift-frame serve! resources [entry] codec)]\\n   470\\t     (if (contains? r :yin.k/status)\\n   471\\t       r\\n   472\\t       (assoc r :yin.k/pending (first (:yin.k/pending r)))))))\\n   473\\t\\n   474\\t\\n   475\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   476\\t;; Lower: back into resources and a wait-set entry\\n   477\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   478\\t\\n   479\\t(defn- stream-id-of\\n   480\\t  \\\"The fresh resource id the reflection of the stream `identity`\\n   481\\t   names stands under: derived from the identity, so two markers of\\n   482\\t   one stream attach once and lower shared. A receiver composing\\n   483\\t   these entries into a live `:resources` table re-keys them -- the\\n   484\\t   ids are fresh for the lowered state, the remap mechanical.\\\"\\n   485\\t  [identity]\\n   486\\t  (keyword \\\"yin.k\\\" (str \\\"s-\\\" identity)))\\n   487\\t\\n   488\\t\\n   489\\t(defn- pending-markers\\n   490\\t  \\\"Every stream marker `pending` names beside its cells' -- the\\n   491\\t   target of a put, the request of a retained call, the pair of a\\n   492\\t   link request.\\\"\\n   493\\t  [pending]\\n   494\\t  (case (:yin.k/reason pending)\\n   495\\t    :put [(:yin.k/stream pending)]\\n   496\\t    :ffi-request [(:yin.k/request pending)]\\n   497\\t    (:link-request :link-response)\\n   498\\t    [(:yin.k/request pending)\\n   499\\t     (:yin.k/response pending)]\\n   500\\t    []))\\n   501\\t\\n   502\\t\\n   503\\t(defn- attach-all\\n   504\\t  \\\"One attach per distinct stream identity, each ok installing its\\n   505\\t   reflection under `stream-id-of`'s fresh resource id. The first\\n   506\\t   attach that does not answer ok -- a reflection marked gone\\n   507\\t   included -- refuses the lower as `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming that\\n   508\\t   identity.\\\"\\n   509\\t  [attach! markers]\\n   510\\t  (let [by-id (reduce (fn [m mkr]\\n   511\\t                        (update m (:dao.stream/identity mkr) #(or % mkr)))\\n   512\\t                      {} markers)]\\n   513\\t    (reduce-kv (fn [acc identity mkr]\\n   514\\t                 (if-let [h (lower-marker attach! mkr)]\\n   515\\t                   (let [sid (stream-id-of identity)]\\n   516\\t                     (-> acc\\n   517\\t                         (assoc-in [:streams identity] sid)\\n   518\\t                         (assoc-in [:resources sid] h)))\\n   519\\t                   (reduced (unsatisfied identity))))\\n   520\\t               {:streams {}, :resources {}}\\n   521\\t               by-id)))\\n   522\\t\\n   523\\t\\n   524\\t(defn- cell-resources\\n   525\\t  \\\"The fresh cursor entry each UCF cell lowers to: its carried\\n   526\\t   position, on the reflection of the stream the cell names, under\\n   527\\t   the cell id itself -- two references to one cell share the one\\n   528\\t   entry, and one ref per cell keeps its own (S7.5.3). A\\n   529\\t   response-route cell lowers under the engine's fixed\\n   530\\t   `vm/call-out-cursor-key` instead, the one key the restored\\n   531\\t   response wait reads (`semantic-restore`'s own shape), still naming\\n   532\\t   the emitter's own call-out reflection: the outstanding call routes\\n   533\\t   to the emitter's pair, while the resumer's own pair under the\\n   534\\t   fixed stream keys is never replaced.\\\"\\n   535\\t  [streams cells routes]\\n   536\\t  (into {}\\n   537\\t        (map (fn [[cid cell]]\\n   538\\t               [(if (contains? routes cid)\\n   539\\t                  vm/call-out-cursor-key\\n   540\\t                  cid)\\n   541\\t                {:stream-id (streams (cell-identity cells cid)),\\n   542\\t                 :cursor (:yin.k/position cell)}]))\\n   543\\t        cells))\\n   544\\t\\n   545\\t\\n   546\\t(defn- route-cells\\n   547\\t  \\\"The UCF cell ids a frame's retained requests name as their\\n   548\\t   response route: the cells that lower under the engine's fixed\\n   549\\t   call-out cursor key rather than their own id, so the route's\\n   550\\t   readers -- the restored response wait, a co-waiting `:ffi`\\n   551\\t   response wait -- share the one entry (S7.5.3).\\\"\\n   552\\t  [pendings]\\n   553\\t  (into #{} (keep :yin.k/response-cell) pendings))\\n   554\\t\\n   555\\t\\n   556\\t(defn- cursor-entry-key\\n   557\\t  \\\"The resource id `cid`'s cursor entry lowers under: the cell id\\n   558\\t   itself, except a response-route cell -- it lowers under the\\n   559\\t   engine's fixed `vm/call-out-cursor-key`, the key the restored\\n   560\\t   response wait reads (`semantic-restore`'s own shape).\\\"\\n   561\\t  [routes cid]\\n   562\\t  (if (contains? routes cid) vm/call-out-cursor-key cid))\\n   563\\t\\n   564\\t\\n   565\\t(defn- link-pair-resources\\n   566\\t  \\\"The engine's fixed link keys (`module/link-request-resource`,\\n   567\\t   `module/link-response-resource`) mapped onto the reflections a\\n   568\\t   lowered link wait uses: the engine's sweep retries a\\n   569\\t   `:link-request` by appending at the fixed request key\\n   570\\t   (`module/append-link-request`) and polls a `:link-response` at the\\n   571\\t   fixed response key (`poll-link-response`), so a lowered link wait\\n   572\\t   parks where the engine looks. One pair per task: the identity of\\n   573\\t   each side rides the pending's own markers.\\\"\\n   574\\t  [streams resources pendings]\\n   575\\t  (reduce (fn [acc pending]\\n   576\\t            (if (contains? #{:link-request :link-response}\\n   577\\t                           (:yin.k/reason pending))\\n   578\\t              (let [req-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\\n   579\\t                                            :dao.stream/identity])\\n   580\\t                    resp-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/response\\n   581\\t                                             :dao.stream/identity])\\n   582\\t                    req (get resources (streams req-id))\\n   583\\t                    resp (get resources (streams resp-id))]\\n   584\\t                (if (and req resp)\\n   585\\t                  (assoc acc\\n   586\\t                         module/link-request-resource req,\\n   587\\t                         module/link-response-resource resp)\\n   588\\t                  acc))\\n   589\\t              acc))\\n   590\\t          {}\\n   591\\t          pendings))\\n   592\\t\\n   593\\t\\n   594\\t(defn- lower-one\\n   595\\t  \\\"One pending of S7.4.3, lowered: `{:entry e}` -- the wait-set\\n   596\\t   entry the receiver parks, the caller's register context `ctx`\\n   597\\t   merged verbatim under the stream and cell fields the data\\n   598\\t   rebuilds -- or an outcome carrying `:yin.k/status`, naming the\\n   599\\t   stream identity where one is known. `routes` are the frame's\\n   600\\t   response-route cells (`route-cells`): a wait on one reads the\\n   601\\t   engine's fixed call-out cursor.\\\"\\n   602\\t  [pending ctx streams cells routes]\\n   603\\t  (case (:yin.k/reason pending)\\n   604\\t    :next\\n   605\\t    (let [cid (:yin.k/cell pending)]\\n   606\\t      (if-let [sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))]\\n   607\\t        {:entry (merge ctx\\n   608\\t                       {:reason :next,\\n   609\\t                        :stream-id sid,\\n   610\\t                        :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref,\\n   611\\t                                     :id (cursor-entry-key routes cid)}})}\\n   612\\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\\n   613\\t\\n   614\\t    :put\\n   615\\t    (if-let [sid (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/stream\\n   616\\t                                           :dao.stream/identity]))]\\n   617\\t      {:entry (merge ctx\\n   618\\t                     {:reason :put,\\n   619\\t                      :stream-id sid,\\n   620\\t                      :datom (:yin.k/value pending)})}\\n   621\\t      (unsatisfied (get-in pending [:yin.k/stream :dao.stream/identity])))\\n   622\\t\\n   623\\t    :ffi\\n   624\\t    (let [cid (:yin.k/cell pending)\\n   625\\t          cursor-id (cursor-entry-key routes cid)]\\n   626\\t      (if-let [sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))]\\n   627\\t        {:entry (merge ctx\\n   628\\t                       (cond-> {:reason :next,\\n   629\\t                                :call-id (:yin.k/call-id pending),\\n   630\\t                                :stream-id sid,\\n   631\\t                                :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref,\\n   632\\t                                             :id cursor-id}}\\n   633\\t                         (contains? pending :yin.k/op)\\n   634\\t                         (assoc :op (:yin.k/op pending))))}\\n   635\\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\\n   636\\t\\n   637\\t    :ffi-request\\n   638\\t    (let [req-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\\n   639\\t                                  :dao.stream/identity])\\n   640\\t          route-id (cell-identity cells (:yin.k/response-cell\\n   641\\t                                          pending))]\\n   642\\t      (if (and (streams req-id) (streams route-id))\\n   643\\t        {:entry (merge ctx\\n   644\\t                       {:reason :put,\\n   645\\t                        :request-sent true,\\n   646\\t                        :call-id (:yin.k/call-id pending),\\n   647\\t                        :op (:yin.k/request-op pending),\\n   648\\t                        :stream-id (streams req-id),\\n   649\\t                        :datom (apply2/request (:yin.k/call-id pending)\\n   650\\t                                               (:yin.k/request-op\\n   651\\t                                                 pending)\\n   652\\t                                               (:yin.k/request-args\\n   653\\t                                                 pending))})}\\n   654\\t        (unsatisfied (if (streams req-id) route-id req-id))))\\n   655\\t\\n   656\\t    (:link-request :link-response)\\n   657\\t    (let [reason (:yin.k/reason pending)\\n   658\\t          cid (:yin.k/cell pending)\\n   659\\t          sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))\\n   660\\t          req (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\\n   661\\t                                        :dao.stream/identity]))]\\n   662\\t      (if (and sid req)\\n   663\\t        {:entry (merge ctx\\n   664\\t                       (cond-> {:reason reason,\\n   665\\t                                :link-id (:yin.k/link-id pending),\\n   666\\t                                :name (:yin.k/name pending),\\n   667\\t                                :request module/link-request-resource,\\n   668\\t                                :response module/link-response-resource,\\n   669\\t                                :cursor (:yin.k/position (get cells cid))}\\n   670\\t                         (= :link-request reason)\\n   671\\t                         (assoc :envelope (:yin.k/envelope pending))))}\\n   672\\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\\n   673\\t\\n   674\\t    :install\\n   675\\t    {:entry (merge ctx\\n   676\\t                   {:reason :install, :name (:yin.k/name pending)})}\\n   677\\t\\n   678\\t    {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable,\\n   679\\t     :yin.k/reason (:yin.k/reason pending)}))\\n   680\\t\\n   681\\t\\n   682\\t(defn lower-frame\\n   683\\t  \\\"A whole frame set of S7.4.3 pendings, lowered together:\\n   684\\t   `{:entries [e ...], :resources table}` -- one fresh stream entry\\n   685\\t   per distinct served identity and one fresh cursor entry per\\n   686\\t   distinct UCF cell, two waiters on one cell lowering back into one\\n   687\\t   shared entry and independent cells staying independent (S7.5.3) --\\n   688\\t   with the same `:yin.k/unsatisfied` and `:yin.k/undecodable`\\n   689\\t   outcomes `lift-frame` gives. Where the engine resolves a wait at\\n   690\\t   one of its own fixed resource keys, the lowered reflections stand\\n   691\\t   under exactly those keys: a link wait's pair under\\n   692\\t   `module/link-request-resource` and `module/link-response-resource`,\\n   693\\t   a retained request's route cell as the fixed call-out cursor\\n   694\\t   entry, naming the emitter's own call-out reflection. The resumer's\\n   695\\t   own call pair under the fixed stream keys is never replaced --\\n   696\\t   outstanding calls route to the emitter's pair, future calls to the\\n   697\\t   resumer's own. `contexts`, parallel to `pendings`, is each\\n   698\\t   entry's register context, merged verbatim.\\\"\\n   699\\t  [attach! pendings cells contexts]\\n   700\\t  (let [ms (distinct (remove nil?\\n   430\\t               (get-in done [:resources cid' :cursor]))\\n   431\\t            \\\"with the source's own recovery cursor in the cell\\\"))\\n   432\\t      (testing \\\"no replay and no silent skip: the walk continues\\n   433\\t                from the recovery cursor\\\"\\n   434\\t        (let [r (get-in done [:resources (:stream-id (:entry lowered))])\\n   435\\t              recovery (get-in done [:resources cid' :cursor])]\\n   436\\t          (is (= :dao.stream/blocked\\n   437\\t                 (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/next r recovery))))\\n   438\\t          (serve-mirror! peer)\\n   439\\t          (let [ok (stream/next r recovery)]\\n   440\\t            (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome ok)))\\n   441\\t            (is (= \\\"v2\\\" (:dao.stream/value ok)))))))))\\n   442\\t\\n   443\\t\\n   444\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   445\\t;; The fixed keys: lowered link waits and retained FFI requests\\n   446\\t;; resume through the engine's own poll and retry paths\\n   447\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   448\\t\\n   449\\t(deftest a-lowered-link-request-retries-and-resumes-through-the-engine\\n   450\\t  (let [t (toy)\\n   451\\t        peer (served-peer t)\\n   452\\t        serve! (server peer (:channel t) #{:reader :writer})\\n   453\\t        attach! (attacher t)\\n   454\\t        [datoms parked entry req-src resp-src]\\n   455\\t        (parked-requirer 'host.the-module)\\n   456\\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! (:resources parked) entry)\\n   457\\t        pending (:yin.k/pending lifted)\\n   458\\t        lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! pending\\n   459\\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted)\\n   460\\t                                          (registers-of entry))\\n   461\\t        e (:entry lowered)\\n   462\\t        rs (:resources lowered)\\n   463\\t        receiver (quiesced-receiver datoms lowered\\n   464\\t                                    (linked-machine 'host.the-module))]\\n   465\\t    (testing \\\"the machine parked through the engine, envelope retained\\\"\\n   466\\t      (is (vm/blocked? parked))\\n   467\\t      (is (= :link-request (:reason entry)))\\n   468\\t      (is (= module/link-request-resource (:request entry)))\\n   469\\t      (is (= module/link-response-resource (:response entry)))\\n   470\\t      (is (map? (:envelope entry)) \\\"the request the retry appends\\\"))\\n   471\\t    (testing \\\"the lower parks the wait where the engine polls\\\"\\n   472\\t      (is (= module/link-request-resource (:request e))\\n   473\\t          \\\"the retry appends at the engine's fixed request key\\\")\\n   474\\t      (is (= module/link-response-resource (:response e))\\n   475\\t          \\\"the poll reads at the engine's fixed response key\\\")\\n   476\\t      (is (contains? rs (:request e)))\\n   477\\t      (is (contains? rs (:response e))\\n   478\\t          \\\"the pair's reflections stand under the fixed keys\\\"))\\n   479\\t    (testing \\\"the engine's own poll retries and resumes the require\\\"\\n   480\\t      ;; the linker answered before the migration: the response sits\\n   481\\t      ;; on the emitter's response stream, past the kept cursor\\n   482\\t      (stream/append! resp-src\\n   483\\t                      {:status :ok,\\n   484\\t                       :yin.link/id (:link-id entry),\\n   485\\t                       :manifest {:yin.module/name 'host.the-module}})\\n   486\\t      (is (vm/blocked? (vm/run receiver))\\n   487\\t          \\\"first poll: the envelope is retried, the answer not yet read\\\")\\n   488\\t      (let [w0 (:dao.stream/cursor\\n   489\\t                 (stream/cursor req-src :dao.stream/oldest))]\\n   490\\t        (is (= :warmed\\n   491\\t               (:dao.stream/value (stream/next req-src w0)))\\n   492\\t            \\\"reading the warm-up frees the slot the retry needs\\\"))\\n   493\\t      (serve-mirror! peer)\\n   494\\t      (let [c0 (:dao.stream/cursor\\n   495\\t                 (stream/cursor req-src :dao.stream/oldest))\\n   496\\t            r (stream/next req-src c0)]\\n   497\\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\\n   498\\t        (is (= (:envelope entry) (:dao.stream/value r))\\n   499\\t            \\\"the envelope verbatim, appended via the fixed request key\\\"))\\n   500\\t      (let [done (vm/run receiver)]\\n   501\\t        (is (vm/halted? done))\\n   502\\t        (is (= 'host.the-module (vm/value done))\\n   503\\t            \\\"the require resumes with the module's own value\\\")\\n   504\\t        (is (empty? (:wait-set done)))))))\\n   505\\t\\n   506\\t\\n   507\\t(deftest a-retained-ffi-request-migrates-and-the-retry-resumes\\n   508\\t  (let [t (toy)\\n   509\\t        peer (served-peer t)\\n   510\\t        serve! (server peer (:channel t) #{:reader :writer})\\n   511\\t        attach! (attacher t)\\n   512\\t        program (then (call-node :op/echo \\\"hello\\\")\\n   513\\t                      (call-node :op/echo \\\"world\\\"))\\n   514\\t        [datoms parked entry call-in-src call-out-src]\\n   515\\t        (parked-caller program)\\n   516\\t        kept (get-in parked [:resources vm/call-out-cursor-key :cursor])\\n   517\\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! (:resources parked) entry)\\n   518\\t        pending (:yin.k/pending lifted)\\n   519\\t        lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! pending\\n   520\\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted)\\n   521\\t                                          (registers-of entry))\\n   522\\t        e (:entry lowered)\\n   523\\t        rs (:resources lowered)\\n   524\\t        ;; the resumer's own pair: the receiving composition supplies\\n   525\\t        ;; it under the fixed stream keys, the lower never replaces it\\n   526\\t        own-call-in (ring 8)\\n   527\\t        own-call-out (ring 8)\\n   528\\t        own (calling-machine own-call-in own-call-out)\\n   529\\t        own-pair (select-keys (:resources own)\\n   530\\t                              [vm/call-in-stream-key\\n   531\\t                               vm/call-out-stream-key\\n   532\\t                               vm/call-out-cursor-key])\\n   533\\t        receiver (-> (quiesced-receiver datoms lowered own)\\n   534\\t                     (update :resources #(merge own-pair %)))\\n   535\\t        oldest (fn [h]\\n   536\\t                 (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h :dao.stream/oldest)))\\n   537\\t        ;; the emitter's bridge answered the migrated call before the\\n   538\\t        ;; migration: the response sits on the emitter's call-out, past\\n   539\\t        ;; the kept cursor\\n   540\\t        r1 (do (stream/append! call-out-src\\n   541\\t                               (apply2/success-response\\n   542\\t                                 (:call-id entry) \\\"echo!\\\"))\\n   543\\t               ;; phase 1: the engine's sweep retries the request\\n   544\\t               ;; through the route and parks the restored response\\n   545\\t               ;; wait\\n   546\\t               (vm/run receiver))\\n   547\\t        warm-up (stream/next call-in-src (oldest call-in-src))\\n   548\\t        _ (serve-mirror! peer)\\n   549\\t        landed (stream/next call-in-src (oldest call-in-src))\\n   550\\t        ;; phase 2: the migrated call resumes and the program's own\\n   551\\t        ;; next call parks on the receiver's own pair\\n   552\\t        r2 (vm/run r1)\\n   553\\t        b-request (stream/next own-call-in (oldest own-call-in))\\n   554\\t        _ (serve-mirror! peer)\\n   555\\t        crossed (stream/next call-in-src (oldest call-in-src))\\n   556\\t        b-response (apply2/success-response\\n   557\\t                     (apply2/request-id (:dao.stream/value b-request))\\n   558\\t                     \\\"world!\\\")\\n   559\\t        ;; the receiver's own bridge serves the new call on its own\\n   560\\t        ;; pair; the outstanding call has discharged, and pending-call\\n   561\\t        ;; routing and future-call routing are separate stores of\\n   562\\t        ;; state, so the composition re-points its spent route at its\\n   563\\t        ;; own pair\\n   564\\t        _ (stream/append! own-call-out b-response)\\n   565\\t        r3 (vm/run (assoc-in r2\\n   566\\t                             [:resources vm/call-out-cursor-key]\\n   567\\t                             (get own-pair vm/call-out-cursor-key)))]\\n   568\\t    (testing \\\"the machine parked through the engine, request retained\\\"\\n   569\\t      (is (vm/blocked? parked))\\n   570\\t      (is (true? (:request-sent entry)))\\n   571\\t      (is (= vm/call-in-stream-key (:stream-id entry)))\\n   572\\t      (is (apply2/request? (:datom entry))))\\n   573\\t    (testing \\\"the lift carries the response route as a cell\\\"\\n   574\\t      (is (= :yin.k/c-0 (:yin.k/response-cell pending)))\\n   575\\t      (is (= kept\\n   576\\t             (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0 :yin.k/position]))\\n   577\\t          \\\"the emitter's call-out cursor at its kept position\\\"))\\n   578\\t    (testing \\\"the lower routes the outstanding call, not the pair\\\"\\n   579\\t      (is (not= vm/call-in-stream-key (:stream-id e))\\n   580\\t          \\\"the retry does not take the receiver's own call-in key\\\")\\n   581\\t      (is (contains? rs (:stream-id e))\\n   582\\t          \\\"it appends on the emitter's own call-in reflection\\\")\\n   583\\t      (is (not (contains? rs vm/call-in-stream-key)))\\n   584\\t      (is (not (contains? rs vm/call-out-stream-key))\\n   585\\t          \\\"the resumer's own pair is not replaced\\\")\\n   586\\t      (let [route (get rs vm/call-out-cursor-key)]\\n   587\\t        (is (= kept (:cursor route))\\n   588\\t            \\\"the route cell lowers as the restored wait's cursor entry\\\")\\n   589\\t        (is (not= vm/call-out-stream-key (:stream-id route))\\n   590\\t            \\\"naming the emitter's call-out, not the receiver's key\\\")\\n   591\\t        (is (contains? rs (:stream-id route))\\n   592\\t            \\\"which is attached, so the wait resolves it\\\")))\\n   593\\t    (testing \\\"the retried response reaches its waiter, emitter's pair\\\"\\n   594\\t      (is (vm/blocked? r1)\\n   595\\t          \\\"first round: the request is retried, the response not yet\\n   596\\t           read\\\")\\n   597\\t      (is (= :warmed (:dao.stream/value warm-up))\\n   598\\t          \\\"reading the warm-up freed the slot the retry needed\\\")\\n   599\\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome landed)))\\n   600\\t      (is (= (:datom entry) (:dao.stream/value landed))\\n   601\\t          \\\"the retained request verbatim, on the emitter's call-in\\\")\\n   602\\t      (is (vm/blocked? r2)\\n   603\\t          \\\"the migrated call resumes and the program calls again\\\")\\n   604\\t      (is (= :next (:reason (first (:wait-set r2))))\\n   605\\t          \\\"the program's own new call is the one waiting now\\\"))\\n   606\\t    (testing \\\"the new call flows on the receiver's own pair\\\"\\n   607\\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome b-request)))\\n   608\\t      (is (= [\\\"world\\\"] (apply2/request-args (:dao.stream/value b-request)))\\n   609\\t          \\\"the future call's request is on the receiver's own call-in\\\")\\n   610\\t      (is (= :dao.stream/blocked (:dao.stream/outcome crossed))\\n   611\\t          \\\"and nothing crossed to the emitter's call-in\\\"))\\n   612\\t    (testing \\\"the receiver's own bridge answers and the program halts\\\"\\n   613\\t      (is (= \\\"world!\\\" (apply2/response-ok b-response)))\\n   614\\t      (is (vm/halted? r3))\\n   615\\t      (is (= \\\"world!\\\" (vm/value r3)))\\n   616\\t      (is (empty? (:wait-set r3))))))\\n   617\\t\\n   618\\t\\n   619\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   620\\t;; Unsatisfied: an unpublishable cursor, a source that cannot be\\n   621\\t;; served, a gone reflection\\n   622\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   623\\t\\n   624\\t(defn- host-cursor-stream\\n   625\\t  \\\"A handle whose cursors hold a host object -- the case\\n   626\\t   dao.stream.remote.md S2.3 says cannot be served.\\\"\\n   627\\t  []\\n   628\\t  (reify stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\\n   629\\t    (descriptor\\n   630\\t      [_]\\n   631\\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\\n   632\\t       :dao.stream/identity \\\"host-cursor\\\"\\n   633\\t       :dao.stream/descriptor\\n   634\\t       {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\\n   635\\t        :dao.stream/identity \\\"host-cursor\\\"}})\\n   636\\t\\n   637\\t\\n   638\\t    stream/IDaoStreamReader\\n   639\\t\\n   640\\t    (cursor\\n   545\\t### 7.4.3 The pending wait travels as data — complete, and resumable elsewhere\\n   546\\t\\n   547\\tA parked machine was waiting for something. That something is a resource of\\n   548\\tthe emitter's host, and the resumer cannot poll it. `:yin.k/pending` records\\n   549\\tthe wait in resource-independent terms so the resumer can re-establish an\\n   550\\t*equivalent* wait, or decide it cannot. The first draft carried sketches;\\n   551\\tthe set here is exhaustive over §7.4.1's reasons, and each variant carries\\n   552\\teverything a *foreign* resumer needs — including the state the first draft\\n   553\\tleft implicit on the emitter's heap:\\n   554\\t\\n   555\\t```clojure\\n   556\\t;; blocked read (:stream-next)\\n   557\\t{:yin.k/reason   :next\\n   558\\t :yin.k/cell     :yin.k/c-17}          ; the cursor CELL id, §7.5.3 — not a bare position\\n   559\\t\\n   560\\t;; blocked write (:stream-put, or an effectful call's :stream/put)\\n   561\\t{:yin.k/reason   :put\\n   562\\t :yin.k/stream   {:dao.stream/identity … :dao.stream/descriptor …}   ; the target\\n   563\\t :yin.k/value    <encoded>}            ; the retained value — a retry appends THIS, and\\n   564\\t                                       ; without it the wait is not re-establishable\\n   565\\t\\n   566\\t;; FFI call, sent (:ffi-call → ok)\\n   567\\t{:yin.k/reason     :ffi\\n   568\\t :yin.k/call-id    :call-7             ; the :dao.stream.apply/id correlation\\n   569\\t :yin.k/op         :op/add\\n   570\\t :yin.k/request    {:dao.stream/identity … :dao.stream/descriptor …}   ; where the request went\\n   571\\t :yin.k/response   {:dao.stream/identity … :dao.stream/descriptor …}   ; where the answer lands\\n   572\\t :yin.k/cell       :yin.k/c-23         ; the response cursor cell, §7.5.3, at its KEPT position}\\n   573\\t\\n   574\\t;; FFI call, retained (:ffi-call → full): the request is still in hand\\n   575\\t{:yin.k/reason     :ffi-request\\n   576\\t :yin.k/call-id    :call-7\\n   577\\t :yin.k/request-op :op/add\\n   578\\t :yin.k/request-args [<encoded> …]     ; enough to rebuild the envelope verbatim\\n   579\\t :yin.k/request    {identity/descriptor as above}\\n   580\\t :yin.k/response   {identity/descriptor as above}\\n   581\\t :yin.k/cell       :yin.k/c-23}        ; response cell at its kept position\\n   582\\t```\\n   583\\t\\n   584\\tThree rules make these resumable somewhere other than where they were minted:\\n   585\\t\\n   586\\t- **The response position is a kept cursor, never an anchor.** Reattaching\\n   587\\t  at `:oldest` replays responses that belong to other calls; attaching at\\n   588\\t  `:newest` skips past this call's own. The response cell therefore travels\\n   589\\t  at its *kept* position, and the whole task's waiters on that cell travel\\n   590\\t  with it (§7.6.3), so the round-order semantics of `check-wait-set` —\\n   591\\t  waiters sharing a cell consume successive values — are preserved on the\\n   592\\t  resumer exactly. A first poll that observes `gap` is the honest outcome\\n   593\\t  the contract already promises a kept cursor (`dao.stream.md`, *Retention\\n   594\\t  and Gaps*). At migration the composition serves every carried stream\\n   595\\t  cell through `dao.stream.remote.md`: the exporter enters the cell's\\n   596\\t  handle in its table and the cell's stream descriptor becomes a remote\\n   597\\t  descriptor. This is an access path to the original logical stream, not\\n   598\\t  a copied stream with new positions. `dao.stream` itself assumes no\\n   599\\t  network. The mirror serves the source's declared reader and writer\\n   600\\t  surface, preserving its outcome maps and cursor namespace rather than\\n   601\\t  assigning new positions. The cell carries its kept cursor. The receiver\\n   602\\t  attaches a reflection through that descriptor and resumes at the kept\\n   603\\t  cursor. `:yin.k/cursor-profiles` in `:yin.k/requires` names\\n   604\\t  `:dao.stream.remote/v1`, the one profile: a cursor is plain data in the\\n   605\\t  channel's portable domain and the source honors it after\\n   606\\t  serialization, including cursor identity, position, and `gap` outcomes.\\n   607\\t  If the source cannot be entered in a table, preserve the cursor, or\\n   608\\t  keep a channel reachable, lift refuses as `:yin.k/unsatisfied` before\\n   609\\t  minting the value. A reflection marked gone on the receiver is also\\n   610\\t  `:yin.k/unsatisfied`, naming the stream identity. The exporter keeps\\n   611\\t  the entry served under a lease the resumer holds\\n   612\\t  (`dao.stream.remote.md`, section 6). Re-homing a stream is out of\\n   613\\t  scope: serving from the exporter pins the exporter.\\n   614\\t- **Outstanding calls route to the emitter's pair; the resumer's pair is its\\n   615\\t  own.** The reference machine restores a `:request-sent` entry into a\\n   616\\t  response wait through its fixed local store keys (`vm/call-out-stream-key`\\n   617\\t  and friends). A resumer must *not* do that: the outstanding call's\\n   618\\t  response will arrive on the **emitter's** response stream, because that is\\n   619\\t  where the request was sent. The resumer re-establishes the wait against\\n   620\\t  the carried response descriptor and the cell's fresh local key (the cell\\n   621\\t  id remapped per §7.5.3), while calls the resumed program makes *after*\\n   622\\t  lowering use the resumer's own pair under its own keys. Pending-call\\n   623\\t  routing and future-call routing are separate stores of state; conflating\\n   624\\t  them strands the migrated call exactly as the review described.\\n   625\\t- **On resume, the resumer attaches and re-mints.** Attach to every\\n   626\\t  descriptor in the frame, pending, and cells; an attachment resolving to\\n   627\\t  `not-found` is `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the stream identity, never a\\n   628\\t  silent `nil`; a `:put` wait retries its retained value and resumes with it\\n   629\\t  on `ok` (the engine, a woken writer's retry appends and stamps the\\n   630\\t  value), where through a reflection `ok` is acceptance on the outbound\\n   900\\t  for correctness of sharing.\\n   901\\t- A cycle (a value reachable from itself through host identity) is refused\\n   902\\t  as `:yin.k/non-portable` with `:yin.k/kind :cyclic` naming the path. The\\n   903\\t  reference machine cannot produce one — `E` is extended by `merge`, never\\n   904\\t  mutated — so the refusal guards against foreign engines and bridge-returned\\n   905\\t  host structures. Cycles *through ref data* cannot be minted at all and are\\n   906\\t  rejected at decode (§7.5.1); this single representation retires the first\\n   907\\t  draft's two competing ones.\\n   908\\t\\n   909\\tBecause table entries are content-addressed, a carrier that already holds an\\n   910\\tentry (a `dao.jing` intake pool, a DHT replica) need not carry it again, and\\n   911\\ttwo continuations parked from the same closure share its encoding. This is\\n   912\\t`streams-all-the-way-down.md` §6.3's checkpoint-as-published-fold applied to\\n   913\\ta single frame. It is also why §7.3.4 separates `:yin.k/id` (which varies\\n   914\\twith these choices, harmlessly) from `:yin.k/occurrence` (which does not).\\n   915\\t\\n   916\\t**Cursor cells.** A cursor is *observable state with aliasing*: two distinct\\n   917\\tcursor refs may sit at the same position and yet be independently\\n   918\\tadvanceable store entries, while repeated refs to one cursor ref must\\n   919\\tadvance together — `check-wait-set` advances a shared cursor ref before\\n   920\\tpolling the next waiter, so waiters on one ref read successive values, and\\n   921\\twaiters on two refs at the same position read the same next value\\n   922\\t(`yin.vm.engine`, `check-wait-set`). A position-only encoding erases\\n   923\\texactly this distinction: two cells at one position would collapse, and\\n   924\\ttheir independent advancement would be lost. The encoding therefore carries\\n   925\\t**logical cursor cells** separately from position content:\\n   926\\t\\n   927\\t```clojure\\n   928\\t:yin.k/cells {:yin.k/c-17 {:yin.k/stream   {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/stream …}\\n   929\\t                           :yin.k/position <opaque, exactly as the transport minted it>}}\\n   930\\t;; values reference cells, never positions:\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"The fixed stream keys are now absent from the lowered resources, and the retry points at a fresh reflection key. I’m checking the remaining cursor-key mapping against shared waiters and the receiver’s next call.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc | sed -n '1,180p;240,460p;682,755p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '85,125p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '500,540p'; rg -n 'call-out-cursor-key|route-cells|lower-frame|response-cell' test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc | sed -n '1,180p;240,460p;682,755p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '85,125p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '500,540p'; rg -n 'call-out-cursor-key|route-cells|lower-frame|response-cell' test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.remote\\n     2\\t  \\\"The UCF facade through `dao.stream.remote` descriptors: lifts a\\n     3\\t   parked semantic machine's pending wait\\n     4\\t   (`docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` S7.4.3) into\\n     5\\t   UCF data whose cells and stream markers name `dao.stream.remote`\\n     6\\t   descriptors under the `:dao.stream.remote/v1` cursor profile\\n     7\\t   (S7.5.3), and lowers that data back into a resumable local wait\\n     8\\t   through a reflection (`docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md` S2.2,\\n     9\\t   S2.4).\\n    10\\t\\n    11\\t   The local side is the engine's own parked machinery, not an\\n    12\\t   invented shape. A pending entry is what `yin.vm` parks: the\\n    13\\t   machine registers beside `:stream-id` and `:cursor-ref`\\n    14\\t   (`yin.vm.semantic` S3.5's park entries, `response-wait-entry`;\\n    15\\t   `yin.vm.engine`'s wait-set sweep), every handle and cursor\\n    16\\t   resolved out of the machine's private `:resources` table -- the\\n    17\\t   lift reads the table, and no entry ever carries a live handle.\\n    18\\t   The lower mirrors it: fresh resource entries, one per stream\\n    19\\t   reflection and one per cursor cell (two waiters sharing one cell\\n    20\\t   share the one entry, S7.5.3), and wait-set entries that merge the\\n    21\\t   caller's register context verbatim, so a lowered wait parks under\\n    22\\t   the engine's own sweep exactly as an unmigrated one does.\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\t   Where the engine polls a wait at one of its own fixed resource\\n    25\\t   keys, the lower parks the wait there: a link wait's pair under\\n    26\\t   `yin.vm.module`'s link-request-resource and\\n    27\\t   link-response-resource, reflections and entry fields alike, and a\\n    28\\t   retained request's response route as the call-out cursor cell the\\n    29\\t   restored response wait reads (`vm/call-out-cursor-key`), naming\\n    30\\t   the emitter's own call-out reflection. The resumer's own call pair\\n    31\\t   under `vm/call-in-stream-key` and `vm/call-out-stream-key` is the\\n    32\\t   composition's own supply and is never replaced: the outstanding\\n    33\\t   call routes to the emitter's pair, future calls of the resumed\\n    34\\t   program to the resumer's own.\\n    35\\t\\n    36\\t   `lift-pending` and `lower-pending` are plain-data functions,\\n    37\\t   parameterized by two composition callbacks rather than coupled to\\n    38\\t   `yin.vm` or `dao.stream.remote` internals:\\n    39\\t\\n    40\\t     serve!  : handle -> {:dao.stream/identity id\\n    41\\t                          :dao.stream/channel chan} | nil\\n    42\\t               the exporter's own table entry\\n    43\\t               (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.3): nil when the handle\\n    44\\t               cannot be served -- no table to enter it in, no\\n    45\\t               channel to the resumer -- which refuses the lift as\\n    46\\t               `:yin.k/unsatisfied` before minting the value\\n    47\\t               (S7.4.3).\\n    48\\t\\n    49\\t     attach! : remote-descriptor -> {:dao.stream/outcome\\n    50\\t                                     :dao.stream/ok\\n    51\\t                                     :dao.stream/handle reflection}\\n    52\\t               | outcome-map\\n    53\\t               the receiver's own `:dao.stream/attach` dispatch for\\n    54\\t               `:dao.stream/remote` (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.4): an\\n    55\\t               outcome other than `ok` -- including a reflection\\n    56\\t               already marked gone -- refuses the lower as\\n    57\\t               `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the stream identity.\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\t   The `:dao.stream.remote/v1` claim is checked, not declared: a cell\\n    60\\t   is published only after its kept cursor survives a round trip\\n    61\\t   through the channel codec -- encoded, decoded back, equal -- which\\n    62\\t   is what plain data in the channel's portable domain means\\n    63\\t   (S7.4.3; `dao.stream.remote.md` S2.3's plain-data basis).\\n    64\\t   `cursor-codec` is the default codec; a composition whose channel\\n    65\\t   speaks another passes its own `{:encode f :decode f}` to\\n    66\\t   `lift-pending` or `lift-frame`. A cursor that does not round trip\\n    67\\t   -- a host object inside is the case S2.3 names -- refuses the lift\\n    68\\t   as `:yin.k/unsatisfied` before any value is minted.\\n    69\\t\\n    70\\t   Every pending variant of S7.4.3 lifts and lowers: `:next`, `:put`,\\n    71\\t   `:ffi`, `:ffi-request`, and the linker's `:link-request`,\\n    72\\t   `:link-response` and `:install` (`yin.vm.linker.md` S7.2-7.3).\\n    73\\t   `:install` names no stream and passes through unchanged.\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\t   Scope: `lift-frame` and `lower-frame` are the frame-level entry\\n    76\\t   points -- cells are minted and remapped across the WHOLE entry\\n    77\\t   set, so two waiters on one engine cursor cell lift to one UCF\\n    78\\t   cell and lower back into one shared cursor entry, and independent\\n    79\\t   cells stay independent (S7.5.3, and the sharing rule of the S7.11\\n    80\\t   pending-state blocker). `lift-pending` and `lower-pending` lift or\\n    81\\t   lower one entry into a self-contained table.\\\"\\n    82\\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\\n    83\\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\\n    84\\t            [dao.stream.cbor :as cbor]\\n    85\\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\\n    86\\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\t(def cursor-profiles\\n    90\\t  \\\"The one portable cursor profile S7.4.3 names in :yin.k/requires: a\\n    91\\t   cursor is plain data in the channel's portable domain and the\\n    92\\t   source honors it after serialization, cursor identity, position and\\n    93\\t   `gap` outcomes included.\\\"\\n    94\\t  #{:dao.stream.remote/v1})\\n    95\\t\\n    96\\t\\n    97\\t(def cursor-codec\\n    98\\t  \\\"The channel codec a lift round-trips kept cursors through when the\\n    99\\t   composition supplies none: the DaoStream v2 wire codec, whose\\n   100\\t   portable domain is the domain the profile claim names.\\\"\\n   101\\t  {:encode cbor/encode, :decode cbor/decode})\\n   102\\t\\n   103\\t\\n   104\\t(def ^:private requires\\n   105\\t  {:yin.k/cursor-profiles cursor-profiles})\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t\\n   108\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   109\\t;; Markers (S7.5.1), through a remote descriptor\\n   110\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   111\\t\\n   112\\t(defn- local-identity\\n   113\\t  \\\"The identity `h` itself declares, when its descriptor answers ok;\\n   114\\t   nil otherwise -- the best name a refusal can give when `serve!` has\\n   115\\t   not minted one.\\\"\\n   116\\t  [h]\\n   117\\t  (let [d (when (stream/descriptor? h) (stream/descriptor h))]\\n   118\\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome d))\\n   119\\t      (:dao.stream/identity d))))\\n   120\\t\\n   121\\t\\n   122\\t(defn- unsatisfied\\n   123\\t  ([] (unsatisfied nil))\\n   124\\t  ([identity]\\n   125\\t   (cond-> {:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied}\\n   126\\t     (some? identity) (assoc :dao.stream/identity identity))))\\n   127\\t\\n   128\\t\\n   129\\t(defn- portable-cursor\\n   130\\t  \\\"The kept cursor when it survives a round trip through the channel\\n   131\\t   codec -- encoded, decoded back, and equal -- which is what the\\n   132\\t   `:dao.stream.remote/v1` claim means: plain data in the channel's\\n   133\\t   portable domain, honored after serialization. nil when it does\\n   134\\t   not, so no cell is ever published over an unpublishable cursor.\\\"\\n   135\\t  [codec cursor]\\n   136\\t  (try (let [w (:encode codec)\\n   137\\t             b (w cursor)\\n   138\\t             r ((:decode codec) b)]\\n   139\\t         (when (= cursor r) cursor))\\n   140\\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\\n   141\\t\\n   142\\t\\n   143\\t(defn lift-marker\\n   144\\t  \\\"The UCF stream marker (S7.5.1) for local handle `h`, its descriptor\\n   145\\t   the remote descriptor `serve!` mints by entering `h` in the\\n   146\\t   exporter's table (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.2). nil when `serve!`\\n   147\\t   refuses -- the source cannot be entered, or cannot honor the\\n   148\\t   profile -- so a caller mints `:yin.k/unsatisfied` before any value\\n   149\\t   is produced (S7.4.3).\\\"\\n   150\\t  [serve! h]\\n   151\\t  (when-let [served (serve! h)]\\n   152\\t    (let [id (:dao.stream/identity served)]\\n   153\\t      {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/stream,\\n   154\\t       :dao.stream/identity id,\\n   155\\t       :dao.stream/descriptor\\n   156\\t       {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote,\\n   157\\t        :dao.stream/identity id,\\n   158\\t        :dao.stream/channel (:dao.stream/channel served)}})))\\n   159\\t\\n   160\\t\\n   161\\t(defn lower-marker\\n   162\\t  \\\"The local handle `attach!` gives for UCF stream marker `m` -- a\\n   163\\t   reflection on the original logical stream -- or nil when the attach\\n   164\\t   does not answer ok: a reflection marked gone, or any other refusal,\\n   165\\t   is unsatisfied at the caller.\\\"\\n   166\\t  [attach! m]\\n   167\\t  (let [result (attach! (:dao.stream/descriptor m))]\\n   168\\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\\n   169\\t      (:dao.stream/handle result))))\\n   170\\t\\n   171\\t\\n   172\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   173\\t;; The pending wait (S7.4.3)\\n   174\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   175\\t;;\\n   176\\t;; Local pending-entry shapes this namespace lifts, and lowers back to\\n   177\\t;; -- the engine's own wait-set shapes, plain data resolved through\\n   178\\t;; the machine's `:resources` table:\\n   179\\t;;\\n   180\\t;;   {:reason :next          :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cid}\\n   240\\t(defn- cursor-cell\\n   241\\t  \\\"The engine cursor cell a `:next` entry waits on: `:cursor-ref`'s\\n   242\\t   id into `:resources`, the cursor entry carrying the stream id and\\n   243\\t   the kept cursor (`vm/cursor-entry`). nil when it names nothing.\\\"\\n   244\\t  [resources entry]\\n   245\\t  (let [cid (get-in entry [:cursor-ref :id])\\n   246\\t        cell (get resources cid)]\\n   247\\t    (when (and (some? cid) (map? cell) (contains? cell :stream-id))\\n   248\\t      {:id cid, :stream-id (:stream-id cell), :cursor (:cursor cell)})))\\n   249\\t\\n   250\\t\\n   251\\t(defn- cell-identity\\n   252\\t  \\\"The stream identity a `:yin.k/cells` entry names, for a refusal\\n   253\\t   that names it even when the cell itself never lowered.\\\"\\n   254\\t  [cells cell-id]\\n   255\\t  (get-in cells [cell-id :yin.k/stream :dao.stream/identity]))\\n   256\\t\\n   257\\t\\n   258\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   259\\t;; Lift: one variant each\\n   260\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   261\\t\\n   262\\t(defn- lift-read\\n   263\\t  \\\"S7.4.3's blocked read: the cell `mint` gives for the entry's\\n   264\\t   cursor cell, at its kept position.\\\"\\n   265\\t  [resources mint codec entry]\\n   266\\t  (if-let [cell (cursor-cell resources entry)]\\n   267\\t    (if-let [cid (mint codec (:id cell)\\n   268\\t                       (get resources (:stream-id cell))\\n   269\\t                       (:cursor cell))]\\n   270\\t      {:pending {:yin.k/reason :next, :yin.k/cell cid}, :cell? true}\\n   271\\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity (get resources (:stream-id cell)))))\\n   272\\t    (unsatisfied)))\\n   273\\t\\n   274\\t\\n   275\\t(defn- lift-response-wait\\n   276\\t  \\\"S7.4.3's sent call: a `:next` entry carrying `:call-id`, the\\n   277\\t   response wait `semantic-restore` rebuilds -- the call's\\n   278\\t   correlation beside the response cell at its kept position, so\\n   279\\t   round-order on the cell is preserved on the resumer (S7.4.3).\\n   280\\t   The call's `:op` rides when the entry carries it (the engine's\\n   281\\t   own response wait does not; a caller assembling the frame takes\\n   282\\t   it from the call's parked record).\\\"\\n   283\\t  [resources mint codec entry]\\n   284\\t  (if-let [cell (cursor-cell resources entry)]\\n   285\\t    (if-let [cid (mint codec (:id cell)\\n   286\\t                       (get resources (:stream-id cell))\\n   287\\t                       (:cursor cell))]\\n   288\\t      {:pending (cond-> {:yin.k/reason :ffi,\\n   289\\t                         :yin.k/call-id (:call-id entry),\\n   290\\t                         :yin.k/cell cid}\\n   291\\t                  (contains? entry :op) (assoc :yin.k/op (:op entry))),\\n   292\\t       :cell? true}\\n   293\\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity (get resources (:stream-id cell)))))\\n   294\\t    (unsatisfied)))\\n   295\\t\\n   296\\t\\n   297\\t(defn- lift-write\\n   298\\t  \\\"S7.4.3's blocked write: the target stream's marker and the\\n   299\\t   retained `:datom` -- the value a retry appends, without which the\\n   300\\t   wait is not re-establishable. A put names a stream, never a\\n   301\\t   cursor cell.\\\"\\n   302\\t  [serve! resources entry]\\n   303\\t  (let [h (get resources (:stream-id entry))]\\n   304\\t    (if-let [marker (lift-marker serve! h)]\\n   305\\t      {:pending {:yin.k/reason :put,\\n   306\\t                 :yin.k/stream marker,\\n   307\\t                 :yin.k/value (:datom entry)}}\\n   308\\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity h)))))\\n   309\\t\\n   310\\t\\n   311\\t(defn- call-out-cell\\n   312\\t  \\\"The emitter's call-out cursor cell -- the response route a retained\\n   313\\t   request's retry reads through. Once the request lands, the engine\\n   314\\t   restores the call as a response wait parked on its fixed local\\n   315\\t   call-out keys (`semantic-restore` -> `response-wait-entry`), so\\n   316\\t   the route is the cursor entry under `vm/call-out-cursor-key`,\\n   317\\t   reading the call-out stream under `vm/call-out-stream-key` at its\\n   318\\t   kept position. nil when the composition holds no call pair, which\\n   319\\t   no real retained request does -- the pair is checked before the\\n   320\\t   call parked.\\\"\\n   321\\t  [resources]\\n   322\\t  (let [cursor (get resources vm/call-out-cursor-key)\\n   323\\t        handle (get resources vm/call-out-stream-key)]\\n   324\\t    (when (and (map? cursor) (contains? cursor :stream-id) handle)\\n   325\\t      {:id vm/call-out-cursor-key,\\n   326\\t       :stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key,\\n   327\\t       :cursor (:cursor cursor)})))\\n   328\\t\\n   329\\t\\n   330\\t(defn- lift-retained-request\\n   331\\t  \\\"S7.4.3's retained call: a `:put` entry carrying `:request-sent`,\\n   332\\t   the request the engine holds unsent. The request stream's marker\\n   333\\t   is served, and `:request-op` and `:request-args` are read out of\\n   334\\t   the retained envelope so a resumer rebuilds it verbatim under the\\n   335\\t   call id. The response route rides beside them as a cell: the\\n   336\\t   emitter's call-out cursor (`call-out-cell`) at its kept position --\\n   337\\t   once the retry lands, the response is read on the emitter's\\n   338\\t   call-out stream through it, so a resumer without the cell strands\\n   339\\t   the restored response wait. The cell shares by identity like any\\n   340\\t   other: a response wait on the same call-out cursor lifts to it too\\n   341\\t   (S7.5.3). `:yin.k/unsatisfied` when the request stream cannot be\\n   342\\t   served, or the route is missing or its cursor does not survive the\\n   343\\t   codec round trip.\\\"\\n   344\\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\\n   345\\t  (let [h (get resources (:stream-id entry))\\n   346\\t        envelope (:datom entry)\\n   347\\t        route (call-out-cell resources)]\\n   348\\t    (if-let [cid (when route\\n   349\\t                   (mint codec (:id route)\\n   350\\t                         (get resources (:stream-id route))\\n   351\\t                         (:cursor route)))]\\n   352\\t      (if-let [marker (lift-marker serve! h)]\\n   353\\t        {:pending {:yin.k/reason :ffi-request,\\n   354\\t                   :yin.k/call-id (:call-id entry),\\n   355\\t                   :yin.k/request-op (or (apply2/request-op envelope)\\n   356\\t                                         (:op entry)),\\n   357\\t                   :yin.k/request-args (apply2/request-args envelope),\\n   358\\t                   :yin.k/request marker,\\n   359\\t                   :yin.k/response-cell cid},\\n   360\\t         :cell? true}\\n   361\\t        (unsatisfied (local-identity h)))\\n   362\\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity\\n   363\\t                     (or (and route (get resources (:stream-id route)))\\n   364\\t                         h))))))\\n   365\\t\\n   366\\t\\n   367\\t(defn- lift-link\\n   368\\t  \\\"S7.4.3's link variants: the link pair name the engine's own fixed\\n   369\\t   link keys on a real entry (`module/link-request-resource` and\\n   370\\t   `module/link-response-resource`), resolved into `:resources`, and\\n   371\\t   the kept `:cursor` on the response stream\\n   372\\t   (`module/require-handler` mints it before the envelope is appended)\\n   373\\t   is the response cell -- a cell like any other, at its kept\\n   374\\t   position. Both pair markers travel, the engine's `:link-response`\\n   375\\t   entry retaining its `:request` beside the response side; the\\n   376\\t   envelope rides verbatim on the request-in-hand variant.\\\"\\n   377\\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\\n   378\\t  (let [reason (:reason entry)\\n   379\\t        resp-h (get resources (:response entry))\\n   380\\t        req-h (get resources (:request entry))\\n   381\\t        kept (:cursor entry)]\\n   382\\t    (if-let [cid (mint codec [(:response entry) kept] resp-h kept)]\\n   383\\t      (let [resp (lift-marker serve! resp-h)\\n   384\\t            req (lift-marker serve! req-h)]\\n   385\\t        (if (and resp req)\\n   386\\t          {:pending (cond-> {:yin.k/reason reason,\\n   387\\t                             :yin.k/link-id (:link-id entry),\\n   388\\t                             :yin.k/name (:name entry),\\n   389\\t                             :yin.k/request req,\\n   390\\t                             :yin.k/response resp,\\n   391\\t                             :yin.k/cell cid}\\n   392\\t                      (= :link-request reason)\\n   393\\t                      (assoc :yin.k/envelope (:envelope entry))),\\n   394\\t           :cell? true}\\n   395\\t          (unsatisfied (local-identity (or req-h resp-h)))))\\n   396\\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity resp-h)))))\\n   397\\t\\n   398\\t\\n   399\\t(defn- lift-one\\n   400\\t  \\\"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lifted into `{:pending data,\\n   401\\t   :cell? bool}` -- `:cell?` true when the variant names a cursor\\n   402\\t   cell, which is what puts `:dao.stream.remote/v1` in\\n   403\\t   `:yin.k/cursor-profiles` -- or an outcome carrying\\n   404\\t   `:yin.k/status`: `:yin.k/unsatisfied` when a stream cannot be\\n   405\\t   served or a kept cursor does not survive the codec round trip;\\n   406\\t   `:yin.k/undecodable`, naming the reason, when the entry is no\\n   407\\t   variant at all.\\\"\\n   408\\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\\n   409\\t  (case (:reason entry)\\n   410\\t    :next\\n   411\\t    (if (:call-id entry)\\n   412\\t      (lift-response-wait resources mint codec entry)\\n   413\\t      (lift-read resources mint codec entry))\\n   414\\t\\n   415\\t    :put\\n   416\\t    (if (:request-sent entry)\\n   417\\t      (lift-retained-request serve! resources mint codec entry)\\n   418\\t      (lift-write serve! resources entry))\\n   419\\t\\n   420\\t    :link-request (lift-link serve! resources mint codec entry)\\n   421\\t\\n   422\\t    :link-response (lift-link serve! resources mint codec entry)\\n   423\\t\\n   424\\t    :install\\n   425\\t    {:pending {:yin.k/reason :install, :yin.k/name (:name entry)}}\\n   426\\t\\n   427\\t    {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable, :yin.k/reason (:reason entry)}))\\n   428\\t\\n   429\\t\\n   430\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   431\\t;; Lift: the frame and the single entry\\n   432\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   433\\t\\n   434\\t(defn lift-frame\\n   435\\t  \\\"A whole frame set of S7.4.3 pending entries, lifted together:\\n   436\\t   `{:yin.k/pending [data ...], :yin.k/cells {cell-id cell},\\n   437\\t   :yin.k/requires requires}` on success -- the cells minted across\\n   438\\t   the WHOLE set, so two waiters on one engine cursor cell lift to\\n   439\\t   one UCF cell (S7.5.3) and `:dao.stream.remote/v1` rides in\\n   440\\t   `:yin.k/cursor-profiles` when any entry names a cell; the S7.9\\n   441\\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` outcome, naming the stream identity where one\\n   442\\t   is known, when any entry's stream cannot be served or its kept\\n   443\\t   cursor does not survive the codec round trip; the S7.9\\n   444\\t   `:yin.k/undecodable` outcome when any entry names no variant.\\n   445\\t   Failure is total (S7.5.4): a refused leaf refuses the frame.\\\"\\n   446\\t  ([serve! resources entries]\\n   447\\t   (lift-frame serve! resources entries cursor-codec))\\n   448\\t  ([serve! resources entries codec]\\n   449\\t   (let [found (atom {:cells {}, :of {}})\\n   450\\t         mint (mint-cell serve! found)\\n   451\\t         lifted (mapv #(lift-one serve! resources mint codec %) entries)]\\n   452\\t     (if-let [refusal (some #(when (contains? % :yin.k/status) %) lifted)]\\n   453\\t       refusal\\n   454\\t       {:yin.k/pending (mapv :pending lifted),\\n   455\\t        :yin.k/cells (:cells @found),\\n   456\\t        :yin.k/requires (if (some :cell? lifted) requires {})}))))\\n   457\\t\\n   458\\t\\n   459\\t(defn lift-pending\\n   460\\t  \\\"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lifted into its own self-contained\\n   682\\t(defn lower-frame\\n   683\\t  \\\"A whole frame set of S7.4.3 pendings, lowered together:\\n   684\\t   `{:entries [e ...], :resources table}` -- one fresh stream entry\\n   685\\t   per distinct served identity and one fresh cursor entry per\\n   686\\t   distinct UCF cell, two waiters on one cell lowering back into one\\n   687\\t   shared entry and independent cells staying independent (S7.5.3) --\\n   688\\t   with the same `:yin.k/unsatisfied` and `:yin.k/undecodable`\\n   689\\t   outcomes `lift-frame` gives. Where the engine resolves a wait at\\n   690\\t   one of its own fixed resource keys, the lowered reflections stand\\n   691\\t   under exactly those keys: a link wait's pair under\\n   692\\t   `module/link-request-resource` and `module/link-response-resource`,\\n   693\\t   a retained request's route cell as the fixed call-out cursor\\n   694\\t   entry, naming the emitter's own call-out reflection. The resumer's\\n   695\\t   own call pair under the fixed stream keys is never replaced --\\n   696\\t   outstanding calls route to the emitter's pair, future calls to the\\n   697\\t   resumer's own. `contexts`, parallel to `pendings`, is each\\n   698\\t   entry's register context, merged verbatim.\\\"\\n   699\\t  [attach! pendings cells contexts]\\n   700\\t  (let [ms (distinct (remove nil?\\n   701\\t                             (concat (map :yin.k/stream (vals cells))\\n   702\\t                                     (mapcat pending-markers pendings))))\\n   703\\t        a (attach-all attach! ms)]\\n   704\\t    (if (contains? a :yin.k/status)\\n   705\\t      a\\n   706\\t      (let [routes (route-cells pendings)\\n   707\\t            lowered (mapv #(lower-one %1 %2 (:streams a) cells routes)\\n   708\\t                          pendings contexts)]\\n   709\\t        (if-let [refusal (some #(when (contains? % :yin.k/status) %)\\n   710\\t                               lowered)]\\n   711\\t          refusal\\n   712\\t          {:entries (mapv :entry lowered),\\n   713\\t           :resources (merge (:resources a)\\n   714\\t                             (cell-resources (:streams a) cells routes)\\n   715\\t                             (link-pair-resources (:streams a)\\n   716\\t                                                  (:resources a)\\n   717\\t                                                  pendings))})))))\\n   718\\t\\n   719\\t\\n   720\\t(defn lower-pending\\n   721\\t  \\\"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lowered: `{:entry e, :resources\\n   722\\t   table}` -- the wait-set entry `ctx`'s registers ride on, and the\\n   723\\t   fresh resource entries it polls through -- with the same\\n   724\\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` and `:yin.k/undecodable` outcomes\\n   725\\t   `lower-frame` gives. Frame assembly that shares cursor entries\\n   726\\t   across entries is `lower-frame`'s.\\\"\\n   727\\t  [attach! pending cells ctx]\\n   728\\t  (let [r (lower-frame attach! [pending] cells [ctx])]\\n   729\\t    (if (contains? r :yin.k/status)\\n   730\\t      r\\n   731\\t      (-> r\\n   732\\t          (assoc :entry (first (:entries r)))\\n   733\\t          (dissoc :entries)))))\\n    85\\t\\n    86\\t(defn- put-registers\\n    87\\t  \\\"Write the five registers back into the record. This is the linear machine's\\n    88\\t   cesk-return: the one seam where the running configuration becomes an\\n    89\\t   observable value, and therefore where per-step trace emission (§3.6) will\\n    90\\t   land when telemetry is designed. A nil segment means the machine has no\\n    91\\t   control left, which is the halted state.\\n    92\\t\\n    93\\t   An empty continuation is stored as nil rather than [] so that\\n    94\\t   `engine/ready-for-ingress?`, which asks `(nil? (:k vm))`, sees a machine\\n    95\\t   between evaluations.\\\"\\n    96\\t  [vm seg pc val St E K]\\n    97\\t  (assoc vm\\n    98\\t         :control (when seg {:segment seg, :pc pc})\\n    99\\t         :value val\\n   100\\t         :stack (or St [])\\n   101\\t         :env E\\n   102\\t         :k (if (seq K) K nil)\\n   103\\t         :halted? (and (not (:blocked? vm)) (nil? seg))))\\n   104\\t\\n   105\\t\\n   106\\t(defn- response-wait-entry\\n   107\\t  \\\"The polling wait entry for a sent call awaiting its correlated response:\\n   108\\t   the machine registers {segment pc env stack k} plus the call-out reader\\n   109\\t   fields, in the shape `ffi/call-response-wait-entry` gives the walker.\\\"\\n   110\\t  [seg pc env stack k call-id]\\n   111\\t  {:segment seg, :pc pc, :env env, :stack stack, :k k,\\n   112\\t   :call-id call-id,\\n   113\\t   :reason :next,\\n   114\\t   :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id vm/call-out-cursor-key},\\n   115\\t   :stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key})\\n   116\\t\\n   117\\t\\n   118\\t(defn semantic-restore\\n   119\\t  \\\"Restore a wait-set or ready-queue entry into machine registers.\\n   120\\t\\n   121\\t   Two entry shapes carry more than registers:\\n   122\\t\\n   123\\t   - A `:request-sent` entry is a writer whose retained FFI request has now\\n   124\\t     been appended. The call starts waiting for its correlated response,\\n   125\\t     exactly as an immediately-sent one does, so the entry is replaced by its\\n   500\\t   over {ok} and wakes nothing: a reader parked on this stream learns of\\n   501\\t   the close from its own next `next`.\\n   502\\t   Returns {:state s'}.\\\"\\n   503\\t  [state effect]\\n   504\\t  (let [stream-id (check-ref! state :stream/close :stream-ref (:stream effect))]\\n   505\\t    (stream/close! (get (:resources state) stream-id))\\n   506\\t    {:state state}))\\n   507\\t\\n   508\\t\\n   509\\t(def ^:private waitset-resolver\\n   510\\t  \\\"The engine's composition for `dao.stream.waitset/check`: the whole\\n   511\\t   resolver contract in one value, both functions synchronous and pure over\\n   512\\t   the immutable resources table. Neither touches a transport -- the\\n   513\\t   library polls, the engine maps.\\n   514\\t\\n   515\\t   `:resolve` maps one whole parked entry to its live handle plus the\\n   516\\t   cursor to read from -- or the value to append -- out of the VM's\\n   517\\t   `:resources`. The cursor is re-resolved on every round even when an\\n   518\\t   earlier round baked a value into the entry: another waiter on the same\\n   519\\t   cursor-ref may have advanced the cell since. `:advance` commits a woken\\n   520\\t   reader's successor -- or recovery -- cursor to its cell before later\\n   521\\t   entries resolve, so a shared cursor-ref advances within the round.\\\"\\n   522\\t  {:resolve (fn [resources entry]\\n   523\\t              (if-let [cursor-ref (:cursor-ref entry)]\\n   524\\t                (let [cursor-data (get resources (:id cursor-ref))]\\n   525\\t                  {:stream (or (:stream entry)\\n   526\\t                               (get resources (:stream-id cursor-data)))\\n   527\\t                   :cursor (:cursor cursor-data)})\\n   528\\t                {:stream (or (:stream entry) (get resources (:stream-id entry)))\\n   529\\t                 :value (:datom entry)}))\\n   530\\t   :advance (fn [resources entry cursor]\\n   531\\t              (let [cursor-id (:id (:cursor-ref entry))]\\n   532\\t                (if cursor-id\\n   533\\t                  (assoc-in resources [cursor-id :cursor] cursor)\\n   534\\t                  resources)))})\\n   535\\t\\n   536\\t\\n   537\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   538\\t;; Lift and lower: the portable encoding a linked slice crosses in\\n   539\\t;; (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, acts 1 and 4; UCF section 7.5.1)\\n   540\\t;; =============================================================================\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:516:        kept (get-in parked [:resources vm/call-out-cursor-key :cursor])\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:532:                               vm/call-out-cursor-key])\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:566:                             [:resources vm/call-out-cursor-key]\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:567:                             (get own-pair vm/call-out-cursor-key)))]\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:574:      (is (= :yin.k/c-0 (:yin.k/response-cell pending)))\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:586:      (let [route (get rs vm/call-out-cursor-key)]\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:758:          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-frame attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:799:          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-frame attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:920:                   vm/call-out-cursor-key\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:931:    (is (= :yin.k/c-0 (:yin.k/response-cell pending))\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:957:      (let [route (get rs vm/call-out-cursor-key)\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:29:   restored response wait reads (`vm/call-out-cursor-key`), naming\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:75:   Scope: `lift-frame` and `lower-frame` are the frame-level entry\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:316:   the route is the cursor entry under `vm/call-out-cursor-key`,\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:322:  (let [cursor (get resources vm/call-out-cursor-key)\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:325:      {:id vm/call-out-cursor-key,\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:359:                   :yin.k/response-cell cid},\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:530:   `vm/call-out-cursor-key` instead, the one key the restored\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:539:                  vm/call-out-cursor-key\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:546:(defn- route-cells\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:553:  (into #{} (keep :yin.k/response-cell) pendings))\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:559:   engine's fixed `vm/call-out-cursor-key`, the key the restored\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:562:  (if (contains? routes cid) vm/call-out-cursor-key cid))\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:600:   response-route cells (`route-cells`): a wait on one reads the\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:640:          route-id (cell-identity cells (:yin.k/response-cell\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:682:(defn lower-frame\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:706:      (let [routes (route-cells pendings)\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:725:   `lower-frame` gives. Frame assembly that shares cursor entries\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:726:   across entries is `lower-frame`'s.\\\"\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:728:  (let [r (lower-frame attach! [pending] cells [ctx])]\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc | sed -n '720,830p;885,980p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '118,155p'; rg -n 'call-out-cursor-key|call-in-stream-key|call-out-stream-key' src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | head -60; cat collab/1790530211570-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice8-fixes-r3.glm-flash.report.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc | sed -n '720,830p;885,980p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '118,155p'; rg -n 'call-out-cursor-key|call-in-stream-key|call-out-stream-key' src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | head -60; cat collab/1790530211570-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice8-fixes-r3.glm-flash.report.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   720\\t                     n))]\\n   721\\t        {:dao.stream/identity id, :dao.stream/channel chan}))))\\n   722\\t\\n   723\\t\\n   724\\t(defn- stub-attach!\\n   725\\t  \\\"An `attach!` that answers ok at once with a reflection standing for\\n   726\\t   the descriptor's identity -- opaque here, since these variants\\n   727\\t   never poll it.\\\"\\n   728\\t  []\\n   729\\t  (fn [d]\\n   730\\t    {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\\n   731\\t     :dao.stream/handle [:reflection-of (:dao.stream/identity d)]}))\\n   732\\t\\n   733\\t\\n   734\\t(def ^:private chan\\n   735\\t  {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel, :dao.stream/identity \\\"c\\\"})\\n   736\\t\\n   737\\t\\n   738\\t(deftest shared-cursor-cells-lift-and-lower-shared\\n   739\\t  (let [serve! (stub-serve! chan)\\n   740\\t        attach! (stub-attach!)\\n   741\\t        [_datoms parked entry _src] (parked-reader 4)\\n   742\\t        cid (:id (:cursor-ref entry))\\n   743\\t        ;; a second waiter on the SAME engine cursor cell, as\\n   744\\t        ;; check-wait-set's shared-cursor co-waiters hold\\n   745\\t        second (assoc (registers-of entry)\\n   746\\t                      :reason :next,\\n   747\\t                      :stream-id (:stream-id entry),\\n   748\\t                      :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cid},\\n   749\\t                      :pc 42)\\n   750\\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-frame serve! (:resources parked)\\n   751\\t                                      [entry second])]\\n   752\\t    (testing \\\"two waiters on one engine cell lift to one UCF cell\\\"\\n   753\\t      (is (= 1 (count (:yin.k/cells lifted))))\\n   754\\t      (let [[p1 p2] (:yin.k/pending lifted)]\\n   755\\t        (is (= (:yin.k/cell p1) (:yin.k/cell p2))\\n   756\\t            \\\"both waiters name the one cell\\\")))\\n   757\\t    (let [ctxs [(registers-of entry) (registers-of second)]\\n   758\\t          lowered (ucf.remote/lower-frame attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\\n   759\\t                                          