hine registers.\\n   120\\t\\n   121\\t   Two entry shapes carry more than registers:\\n   122\\t\\n   123\\t   - A `:request-sent` entry is a writer whose retained FFI request has now\\n   124\\t     been appended. The call starts waiting for its correlated response,\\n   125\\t     exactly as an immediately-sent one does, so the entry is replaced by its\\n   126\\t     response reader and the machine stays blocked.\\n   127\\t   - A `:call-id` entry is a response reader. The woken value is a response\\n   128\\t     envelope, so `ffi/call-result` unwraps it, checks correlation, and the\\n   129\\t     parked call leaves `:parked` rather than accumulating.\\\"\\n   130\\t  ([base entry] (semantic-restore base entry (:value entry)))\\n   131\\t  ([base entry val]\\n   132\\t   (if (:request-sent entry)\\n   133\\t     (assoc base\\n   134\\t            :wait-set (conj (vec (or (:wait-set base) []))\\n   135\\t                            (response-wait-entry (:segment entry)\\n   136\\t                                                 (:pc entry)\\n   137\\t                                                 (:env entry)\\n   138\\t                                                 (:stack entry)\\n   139\\t                                                 (:k entry)\\n   140\\t                                                 (:call-id entry)))\\n   141\\t            :control nil\\n   142\\t            :k nil\\n   143\\t            :value :yin/blocked\\n   144\\t            :blocked? true\\n   145\\t            :halted? false)\\n   146\\t     (let [call-id (:call-id entry)\\n   147\\t           base (if call-id (update base :parked dissoc call-id) base)\\n   148\\t           val (if call-id (ffi/call-result val call-id) val)]\\n   149\\t       (put-registers base\\n   150\\t                      (:segment entry)\\n   151\\t                      (:pc entry)\\n   152\\t                      val\\n   153\\t                      (:stack entry)\\n   154\\t                      (:env entry)\\n   155\\t                      (:k entry))))))\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:475:(def call-in-stream-key\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:480:(def call-out-stream-key\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:485:(def call-out-cursor-key\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:2043:                   {call-in-stream-key call-in,\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:2044:                    call-out-stream-key call-out,\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:2045:                    call-out-cursor-key (cursor-entry call-out-stream-key\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc:38:  (let [in (get resources vm/call-in-stream-key)\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc:39:        out (get resources vm/call-out-stream-key)]\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc:61:   :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id vm/call-out-cursor-key},\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc:63:   :stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key})\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc:84:             :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id vm/call-out-cursor-key}\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc:85:             :stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key)))\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc:173:  (let [call-out (get (:resources vm) vm/call-out-stream-key)\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc:215:      (let [call-in (get (:resources vm) vm/call-in-stream-key)\\nThe route-cell routing fix (P1 from gate r3).** The wholesale replacement of the receiver's fixed call-pair keys is gone, and the outstanding call now routes to the emitter's pair entirely through non-fixed state:\\n\\n- Deleted `call-pair-resources` outright — `lower-frame` (src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:712-716) no longer installs the emitter's reflected call streams at `vm/call-in-stream-key`/`vm/call-out-stream-key`. Those keys remain the receiving composition's own supply (`ffi/call-pair`, ffi.cljc:33-40), so the resumed program's future FFI calls use the receiver's own pair (UCF §\\\"Outstanding calls route to the emitter's pair; the resumer's pair is its own\\\", yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:614-624).\\n- The lowered `:request-sent` entry's `:stream-id` is the fresh reflection key of the emitter's own call-in (remote.cljc:648) — the retry appends on the emitter's pair without occupying the fixed call-in key (remote.cljc:641-661).\\n- The route cell lowers as the fixed `vm/call-out-cursor-key` entry — the one key the restored response wait reads (`semantic-restore` → `response-wait-entry`, semantic.cljc:106-115) — still naming the emitter's own call-out reflection via its fresh key, not `:yin/call-out` (`cell-resources`, remote.cljc:524-543; `cursor-entry-key`, remote.cljc:556-562 keeps §7.5.3 sharing for co-waiters). Confirmed r2 behavior (link waits on the fixed link keys, remote.cljc:665-668 + `link-pair-resources` remote.cljc:565) is untouched.\\n\\n**Test extended past the migrated call** (test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:507-618, `a-retained-ffi-request-migrates-and-the-retry-resumes`): the program makes two calls — the migrated one and a new one. After the migrated call's response reaches its waiter through the emitter's pair (retry envelope verified landing verbatim on the emitter's call-in via the wire; response consumed via the route cell), the program's new call flows on the receiver's own pair: its request lands on the receiver's own call-in (`[\\\"world\\\"]`, :606-611) and nothing crosses to the emitter's call-in; the receiver's own bridge answers on its own call-out, and after the composition re-points its spent route at its own pair (the doc's separate-stores rule, :561-565), run 3 halts with \\\"world!\\\" and an empty wait-set. The routing assertions (:545-559) pin: no fixed stream keys in the lowered table, retry on the emitter's reflection, route cell naming the emitter's call-out. Debugging used a /tmp scratch script (deleted) — no repo files beyond the two slice-8 files.\\n\\n**Lane counts (focused, exact).**\\n- JVM `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.ucf.remote-test`: Ran 18 tests containing 162 assertions — 0 failures, 0 errors.\\n- Node (shadow-cljs build; `node target/node-tests.js --test=yin.vm.ucf.remote-test`): Ran 18 tests containing 162 assertions — 0 failures, 0 errors.\\n- Dart (`flutter test test/cljd-out/yin/vm/ucf/remote-test_test.dart` on the `cljd`-compiled file): 18 of 18 passed — \\\"All tests passed!\\\".\\n- Attribution: full-suite runs touched other namespaces only — Node full run: 7 failures, all `dao.stream.ws.node-test` (concurrent slice-5 ws/rpc work); Dart full run: 33 loading failures in demo/embed files plus `cljd/flutter.dart` IFnMixin analyzer noise from the shared cljd-out tree mid-flight (slice-5). None in `yin.vm.ucf.remote-test`.\\n- Hygiene: cljstyle check clean, clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings, pure ASCII, ≤ 80 columns, no diagnostics; both slice-8 files still untracked, no git operations.\\n\\nStatus: COMPLETE\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-27 21:20:27 GMT\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-28 04:20:27 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\\n\\n**P1 — the fixed response cursor still misroutes the next call.** The retry now uses the emitter’s fresh call-in reflection, and lowering leaves the receiver’s fixed stream keys free ([remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:637), [remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:712)). But the migrated route occupies `vm/call-out-cursor-key` ([remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:524)). Every new call waits on that key, and the engine resolves its stream from the cursor cell ([semantic.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:106), [engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:522)). The two-call test halts only after it manually replaces the cell with the receiver’s own at [remote_test.cljc:559](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:559). Slice 8 supplies no such handoff.\\n\\n**P1 — distinct response routes collide in a frame.** `route-cells` can collect multiple response-cell IDs, but `cell-resources` maps every one to the same fixed cursor key ([remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:546), [remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:524)). One cell entry overwrites another, so independently advanceable waiters can read one route and cursor. This also prevents a safe blanket replacement of the fixed cell while a co-waiter still uses it; UCF requires shared references to advance together and distinct cells to remain independent ([UCF §7.5.3](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:916)).\\n\\nI made no edits and did not rerun suites. The supplied 18-test, 162-assertion green results on JVM, Node, and Dart cover the tested path, including its manual handoff.\\n\\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\\nSign-off: DENIED\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":209614,\"cached_input_tokens\":177280,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":1555,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":170}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
