{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | sed -n '540,588p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | sed -n '470,490p;2035,2058p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '855,882p'\"","aggregated_output":"   540\t\n   541\tSafepoints are datoms, so a query can ask \"where can this program be\n   542\tmigrated?\" without running it, and a debugger's breakpoint set is a subset of\n   543\tthe safepoint set by construction.\n   544\t\n   545\t### 7.4.3 The pending wait travels as data — complete, and resumable elsewhere\n   546\t\n   547\tA parked machine was waiting for something. That something is a resource of\n   548\tthe emitter's host, and the resumer cannot poll it. `:yin.k/pending` records\n   549\tthe wait in resource-independent terms so the resumer can re-establish an\n   550\t*equivalent* wait, or decide it cannot. The first draft carried sketches;\n   551\tthe set here is exhaustive over §7.4.1's reasons, and each variant carries\n   552\teverything a *foreign* resumer needs — including the state the first draft\n   553\tleft implicit on the emitter's heap:\n   554\t\n   555\t```clojure\n   556\t;; blocked read (:stream-next)\n   557\t{:yin.k/reason   :next\n   558\t :yin.k/cell     :yin.k/c-17}          ; the cursor CELL id, §7.5.3 — not a bare position\n   559\t\n   560\t;; blocked write (:stream-put, or an effectful call's :stream/put)\n   561\t{:yin.k/reason   :put\n   562\t :yin.k/stream   {:dao.stream/identity … :dao.stream/descriptor …}   ; the target\n   563\t :yin.k/value    <encoded>}            ; the retained value — a retry appends THIS, and\n   564\t                                       ; without it the wait is not re-establishable\n   565\t\n   566\t;; FFI call, sent (:ffi-call → ok)\n   567\t{:yin.k/reason     :ffi\n   568\t :yin.k/call-id    :call-7             ; the :dao.stream.apply/id correlation\n   569\t :yin.k/op         :op/add\n   570\t :yin.k/request    {:dao.stream/identity … :dao.stream/descriptor …}   ; where the request went\n   571\t :yin.k/response   {:dao.stream/identity … :dao.stream/descriptor …}   ; where the answer lands\n   572\t :yin.k/cell       :yin.k/c-23         ; the response cursor cell, §7.5.3, at its KEPT position}\n   573\t\n   574\t;; FFI call, retained (:ffi-call → full): the request is still in hand\n   575\t{:yin.k/reason     :ffi-request\n   576\t :yin.k/call-id    :call-7\n   577\t :yin.k/request-op :op/add\n   578\t :yin.k/request-args [<encoded> …]     ; enough to rebuild the envelope verbatim\n   579\t :yin.k/request    {identity/descriptor as above}\n   580\t :yin.k/response   {identity/descriptor as above}\n   581\t :yin.k/cell       :yin.k/c-23}        ; response cell at its kept position\n   582\t```\n   583\t\n   584\tThree rules make these resumable somewhere other than where they were minted:\n   585\t\n   586\t- **The response position is a kept cursor, never an anchor.** Reattaching\n   587\t  at `:oldest` replays responses that belong to other calls; attaching at\n   588\t  `:newest` skips past this call's own. The response cell therefore travels\n   470\t                      {:rule :ambiguous-primitive,\n   471\t                       :names names}))))\n   472\t  primitive-map)\n   473\t\n   474\t\n   475\t(def call-in-stream-key\n   476\t  \"Store key for the shared apply inbound request stream (caller writes, callee reads).\"\n   477\t  :yin/call-in)\n   478\t\n   479\t\n   480\t(def call-out-stream-key\n   481\t  \"Store key for the shared apply outbound response stream (callee writes, caller reads).\"\n   482\t  :yin/call-out)\n   483\t\n   484\t\n   485\t(def call-out-cursor-key\n   486\t  \"Store key for the shared apply outbound stream cursor.\"\n   487\t  :yin/call-out-cursor)\n   488\t\n   489\t\n   490\t(def default-call-capacity\n  2035\t                                     (swap! created conj h)\n  2036\t                                     h))\n  2037\t                       call-out (or supplied-out\n  2038\t                                    (let [h (create-stream! make-stream\n  2039\t                                                            capacity\n  2040\t                                                            :call-out)]\n  2041\t                                      (swap! created conj h)\n  2042\t                                      h))]\n  2043\t                   {call-in-stream-key call-in,\n  2044\t                    call-out-stream-key call-out,\n  2045\t                    call-out-cursor-key (cursor-entry call-out-stream-key\n  2046\t                                                      (mint-oldest call-out\n  2047\t                                                                   :call-out))})\n  2048\t                 (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n  2049\t                   (doseq [h @created] (close-quietly h))\n  2050\t                   (throw e)))))]\n  2051\t       {:store {},\n  2052\t        :resources (cond-> (or pair-store {})\n  2053\t                     (:link-request opts)\n  2054\t                     (assoc :yin.link/request (:link-request opts))\n  2055\t                     (:link-response opts)\n  2056\t                     (assoc :yin.link/response (:link-response opts))),\n  2057\t        :origin (or (:origin opts) :t0),\n  2058\t        :ancestry (vec (:ancestry opts)),\n   855\t  (continuation [vm] (:k vm)))\n   856\t\n   857\t\n   858\t(defn create-vm\n   859\t  \"Create a new SemanticVM.\n   860\t\n   861\t   Options:\n   862\t     :env           initial lexical environment\n   863\t     :primitives    primitive operations map\n   864\t     :primitive-profiles published primitive profile registry\n   865\t     :primitive-canonical-names name -> canonical name for intentional aliases\n   866\t     :modules       module registry value (see `yin.vm.module`)\n   867\t     :make-stream   (fn [capacity] -> create outcome); no default\n   868\t     :call-in       explicit inbound request handle\n   869\t     :call-out      explicit outbound response handle\n   870\t     :call-capacity capacity for a constructed FFI pair\n   871\t     :bridge        host FFI handlers\n   872\t\n   873\t   As for the walker: there is no `:in-stream` (program observation belongs\n   874\t   to `dao.stream.observer`), and construction is all-or-nothing — the FFI\n   875\t   pair and its call-out cursor are stream operations whose failure fails\n   876\t   here.\"\n   877\t  ([] (create-vm {}))\n   878\t  ([opts]\n   879\t   (when (contains? opts :in-stream)\n   880\t     (throw (ex-info\n   881\t              \"Program observation moved to dao.stream.observer: a VM no longer accepts :in-stream\"\n   882\t              {:in-stream (:in-stream opts)})))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
