{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-27 22:16:00 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-28 05:16:00 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\n**P1 — a retained call can resume against a different FFI service.** The lift carries the emitter’s request marker and response cell ([remote.cljc:331](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:331)), but lowering retries on the receiver’s fixed call-in key and leaves the carried response route unused ([remote.cljc:607](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:607)). `semantic-restore` then waits on the receiver’s call-out cursor ([semantic.cljc:132](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:132)). This passes the two-call test because its receiver supplies a compatible echo service; it does not preserve the carried endpoints required for the outstanding call by [UCF §7.4.3](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:574). A receiver with a different FFI handler can return a different result for the migrated call.\n\n**P1 — lowered resource IDs are not fresh across installations.** Each lift starts cell numbering at `:yin.k/c-0` ([remote.cljc:229](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:229)); lowering uses that ID directly as a resource key ([remote.cljc:522](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:522)). Stream keys are likewise derived solely from the served identity ([remote.cljc:477](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:477)). Installing two separately lowered frames in one task can overwrite a cursor cell and change which stream a wait polls. The tests cover sharing and independence *within* one frame ([remote_test.cljc:738](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:738)), but not fresh-key remapping against the receiver’s resource table.\n\nThe fixed-key overwrite from round 5 is removed, and the supplied focused JVM, Node, and Dart results are green. I made no edits and did not rerun suites.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\nSign-off: DENIED"}}
